 cillum nunc dui. Vitae a dolorum, quae placeat erat. Mi ac vivamus, minus ultricies voluptate doloribus neque? Rhoncus anim pharetra proident eveniet doloremque alias quos.<\\/p>\\n<!-- \\/wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list -->\\n<ul>\\n<li>Alias natus commodo facilis.<\\/li>\\n<li>Nihil libero quos aliquet.<\\/li>\\n<li>Eget, phasellus maiores nulla.<\\/li>\\n<li>Cupidatat consequuntur officia saepe.<\\/li>\\n<li>Totam, anim facere commodo.<\\/li>\\n<li>Quos cubilia morbi sequi.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<!-- \\/wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph -->\\n<p>Pariatur ultricies labore! Consequat beatae! Hac varius maxime eveniet pulvinar atque! Luctus! Occaecat sollicitudin doloremque diamlorem praesent odio, impedit sed nullam fugit omnis platea aliquam, voluptatem soluta cupiditate delectus ullam sociis, consectetur, nobis curae dolorem. Parturient faucibus eum assumenda, placerat.<\\/p>\\n<!-- \\/wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph -->\\n<p>Sunt, inceptos tempora adipiscing harum porro error cupidatat? Fusce ullamco amet esse interdum ipsam dolore consequuntur. Elit, nam convallis, wisi? Deserunt dapibus? Condimentum nunc possimus sem! Pede, iusto fuga. Torquent, ipsam facilis, vitae, eget culpa aliqua. Habitasse vero, senectus maiores.<\\/p>\\n<!-- \\/wp:paragraph -->\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1233,793,'_wp_page_template','default'),(1234,793,'_thumbnail_id','1133'),(1235,793,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1236,793,'_elementor_template_type','wp-post'),(1237,793,'_elementor_version','3.28.4'),(1238,793,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"3415c006\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":[],\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"542b4229\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"editor\":\"<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-644be11 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"644be11\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\" data-settings=\\\"{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c134fba elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"c134fba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>Stairs play a crucial role in architecture, offering vertical connectivity between floors in multi-story buildings while fulfilling a functional purpose. Stairs are a structure that allows movement between different levels by dividing the vertical distance into smaller, manageable steps.<\\/p>\\n<p>Stairs encompass staircases, also called stairways, as well as escalators. Alternatives to traditional stairs include elevators (lifts), stair lifts, inclined moving walkways, ladders, and ramps.<\\/p>\\n<p>This article aims to highlight key aspects of stair codes relevant to steel detailing.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1ce422f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"1ce422f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f159939 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"f159939\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2>Table of Contents<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-5e86856 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-mobile__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"5e86856\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section1\\\">Introduction<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section2\\\">Stair Codes and Their Significance <\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section3\\\">Codes and Standards Applicable to Steel Detailing<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section4\\\">Conclusion<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3126a5f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"3126a5f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b99b920 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"b99b920\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section1\\\">1. INTRODUCTION<\\/h2>\\n<div>Stair codes play a vital role in safety, ensuring that stairs are designed to minimize the risk of falls and injuries. These regulations dictate key dimensions such as tread depth, riser height, and handrail specifications, all enforced to safeguard users.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d3ea5c7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"d3ea5c7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section2\\\">2. STAIR CODES AND THEIR IMPORTANCE<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>In the United States, stair detailing must adhere to various codes and standards to ensure safety, accessibility, and structural integrity. These regulations define essential aspects such as tread depth, riser height, handrails, and load-bearing requirements.<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Code Council was established in 1994, with the goal of developing a single set of national model construction codes. It brought together three different organizations that had developed three separate sets of model codes throughout the U.S.: Building Offi\\u00adcials and Code Administrators International, Inc. (BOCA), International Conference of Building Officials (ICBO) and Southern Building Code Congress International, Inc. (SBCCI).<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Building Code (IBC) and International Residential Code (IRC) are model building codes developed by the International Code Council (ICC) that are adopted by many jurisdictions in the US to ensure public safety and welfare in the built environment. The IBC applies to most structures, while the IRC specifically addresses one- and two-family dwellings.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-51aa218 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"51aa218\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section3\\\">3. CODES AND STANDARDS USED IN STEEL DETAILING<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>The following codes are applied in stair detailing:<\\/p>\\n<ol>\\n<li>IBC (International Building Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/li>\\n<li>ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/li>\\n<li>PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d1ec165 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d1ec165\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a49f34d e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"a49f34d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-88bd7bd elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"88bd7bd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5><strong>1. IBC (International Building Code)<\\/strong><\\/h5>\\n<p>The IBC is a model building code that provides a comprehensive set of guidelines for the design, construction, and safety of buildings, with the goal of protecting public health, safety, and welfare.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IBC Requirements for Stairways:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Width and Clearance<\\/strong>: Defines minimum stairway width for safe passage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Tread and Riser Dimensions<\\/strong>: Specifies uniform riser heights and tread depths for comfortable and secure movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Handrails and Guardrails<\\/strong>: Sets rules for placement, height, and design to enhance stability and prevent falls.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing and Platforms<\\/strong>: Regulates landing dimensions to provide resting points and safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Fire Safety and Egress<\\/strong>: Ensures stairways support emergency evacuation routes with proper fire-resistant materials and signage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Accessibility Compliance<\\/strong>: Aligns with ADA guidelines to accommodate users with mobility challenges.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ece6749 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"ece6749\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3421 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"AISC - Design_Guide - STAIR MINIMUM REQUIREMENT SKETCH\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\"><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d20752c e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d20752c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-97c617a elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"97c617a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">2. IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3ea0f4f e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"3ea0f4f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-27a8db1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"27a8db1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The International Residential Code (IRC) sets safety and design standards for stairways in residential buildings, ensuring they meet structural, accessibility, and usability requirements. These guidelines help prevent accidents and improve comfort in homes.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IRC Stairway Regulations:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Maximum Riser Height<\\/strong>: Defines the height of each step to maintain consistency and ease of movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Minimum Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Ensures sufficient foot space for stability while ascending or descending.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1d689e0 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"1d689e0\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3428 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" width=\\\"1024\\\" height=\\\"590\\\"><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f5666db e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"f5666db\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3780e4a elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"3780e4a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Handrail Requirements<\\/strong>: Specifies height and graspability for added safety and support.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Guardrail Standards<\\/strong>: Prevents falls by establishing minimum railing height and spacing.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing Dimensions<\\/strong>: Regulates the size and placement of stair landings for safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Headroom Clearance<\\/strong>: Ensures adequate overhead space to prevent obstructions.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>These IRC rules play a crucial role in designing residential stairways that are both functional and compliant with safety standards.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ce18657 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ce18657\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-adc4321 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"adc4321\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">3. OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-55edcc6 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"55edcc6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-56630d5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"56630d5\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) is a U.S. government agency responsible for ensuring safe and healthy working conditions. Established in 1970 under the Occupational Safety and Health Act, OSHA sets regulations and conducts inspections to protect workers across various industries.<\\/p>\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) standard 1910.25 outlines safety requirements for stairways in workplaces to prevent accidents and ensure structural integrity. These regulations apply to various stair types, including standard, spiral, ship, and alternating tread stairs.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-10bffc2 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"10bffc2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3432 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\"><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ada56dd e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ada56dd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fd0407a e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"fd0407a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0f39eee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"0f39eee\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default elementor-inline-editing pen\\\" spellcheck=\\\"false\\\" data-elementor-setting-key=\\\"title\\\" data-pen-placeholder=\\\"Type Here...\\\" data-qb-tmp-id=\\\"lt-738382\\\" data-gramm=\\\"false\\\" contenteditable=\\\"true\\\">4. ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/h5>\\n<p>The Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) establishes accessibility standards for stairways to ensure safe and inclusive navigation for individuals with disabilities. These regulations apply to both interior and exterior stairs in public buildings and facilities.<br>Key ADA Stairway Requirements:<br><strong>Uniform Step Dimensions<\\/strong>: All steps must have consistent depth and height to prevent tripping hazards.<br><strong>Step Height<\\/strong>: Must be between 5 and 7 inches for accessibility.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Minimum of 11 inches, measured from riser to riser, to provide secure footing.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Stair Width<\\/strong>: Must be at least 36 inches to accommodate users safely.<br><strong>Handrails<\\/strong>: Required on both sides of stairways, positioned 34 to 38 inches above the stair nosing.<br><strong>Nosings<\\/strong>: Must not project more than 1.5 inches beyond the riser below to reduce tripping risks.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-8baa50f elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"8baa50f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><br><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-bbd2929 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"bbd2929\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c40a9f7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"c40a9f7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3469 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\"><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0c64e0e elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"0c64e0e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3465 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\"><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-57c9bd3 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"57c9bd3\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3477 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\"><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-e411696 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"e411696\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2fada2e elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"2fada2e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">5. PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2e1c457 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"2e1c457\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>PIP Civil, Structural, and Architectural (CSA) Practices publishes essential CSA Engineering Design Practices, including specifications and fabrication\\/installation details.<\\/p>\\n<p>This Practice provides fabrication and installation details for standard pipe railing for walking and working surfaces and for stair railing or handrail for egress. Although the details in this practice are intended to meet U.S. Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) requirements for process facilities, they may not meet the requirements of local or national building codes.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-82239ba e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"82239ba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-125261c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"125261c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section4\\\">4. CONCLUSION<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>Building codes for stairs are established to enhance safety for all users, including children, the elderly, and individuals with disabilities.<\\/p>\\n<p>They help minimize the risks of slips, trips, and falls while ensuring uniformity in design and construction for both contractors and homeowners.<\\/p>\\n<p>The codes outlined above play a crucial role in stair design and construction, with periodic updates to accommodate evolving safety standards and requirements.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1240,794,'_wp_page_template','default'),(1241,794,'_thumbnail_id','1133'),(1242,794,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1243,794,'_elementor_template_type','wp-post'),(1244,794,'_elementor_version','3.28.4'),(1245,794,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"3415c006\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":[],\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"542b4229\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"editor\":\"<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-644be11 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"644be11\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\" data-settings=\\\"{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c134fba elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"c134fba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>Stairs play a crucial role in architecture, offering vertical connectivity between floors in multi-story buildings while fulfilling a functional purpose. Stairs are a structure that allows movement between different levels by dividing the vertical distance into smaller, manageable steps.<\\/p>\\n<p>Stairs encompass staircases, also called stairways, as well as escalators. Alternatives to traditional stairs include elevators (lifts), stair lifts, inclined moving walkways, ladders, and ramps.<\\/p>\\n<p>This article aims to highlight key aspects of stair codes relevant to steel detailing.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1ce422f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"1ce422f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f159939 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"f159939\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2>Table of Contents<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-5e86856 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-mobile__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"5e86856\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section1\\\">Introduction<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section2\\\">Stair Codes and Their Significance <\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section3\\\">Codes and Standards Applicable to Steel Detailing<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section4\\\">Conclusion<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3126a5f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"3126a5f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b99b920 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"b99b920\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section1\\\">1. INTRODUCTION<\\/h2>\\n<div>Stair codes play a vital role in safety, ensuring that stairs are designed to minimize the risk of falls and injuries. These regulations dictate key dimensions such as tread depth, riser height, and handrail specifications, all enforced to safeguard users.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d3ea5c7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"d3ea5c7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section2\\\">2. STAIR CODES AND THEIR IMPORTANCE<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>In the United States, stair detailing must adhere to various codes and standards to ensure safety, accessibility, and structural integrity. These regulations define essential aspects such as tread depth, riser height, handrails, and load-bearing requirements.<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Code Council was established in 1994, with the goal of developing a single set of national model construction codes. It brought together three different organizations that had developed three separate sets of model codes throughout the U.S.: Building Offi\\u00adcials and Code Administrators International, Inc. (BOCA), International Conference of Building Officials (ICBO) and Southern Building Code Congress International, Inc. (SBCCI).<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Building Code (IBC) and International Residential Code (IRC) are model building codes developed by the International Code Council (ICC) that are adopted by many jurisdictions in the US to ensure public safety and welfare in the built environment. The IBC applies to most structures, while the IRC specifically addresses one- and two-family dwellings.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-51aa218 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"51aa218\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section3\\\">3. CODES AND STANDARDS USED IN STEEL DETAILING<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>The following codes are applied in stair detailing:<\\/p>\\n<ol>\\n<li>IBC (International Building Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/li>\\n<li>ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/li>\\n<li>PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d1ec165 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d1ec165\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a49f34d e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"a49f34d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-88bd7bd elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"88bd7bd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5><strong>1. IBC (International Building Code)<\\/strong><\\/h5>\\n<p>The IBC is a model building code that provides a comprehensive set of guidelines for the design, construction, and safety of buildings, with the goal of protecting public health, safety, and welfare.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IBC Requirements for Stairways:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Width and Clearance<\\/strong>: Defines minimum stairway width for safe passage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Tread and Riser Dimensions<\\/strong>: Specifies uniform riser heights and tread depths for comfortable and secure movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Handrails and Guardrails<\\/strong>: Sets rules for placement, height, and design to enhance stability and prevent falls.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing and Platforms<\\/strong>: Regulates landing dimensions to provide resting points and safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Fire Safety and Egress<\\/strong>: Ensures stairways support emergency evacuation routes with proper fire-resistant materials and signage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Accessibility Compliance<\\/strong>: Aligns with ADA guidelines to accommodate users with mobility challenges.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ece6749 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"ece6749\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3421 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"AISC - Design_Guide - STAIR MINIMUM REQUIREMENT SKETCH\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\"><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d20752c e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d20752c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-97c617a elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"97c617a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">2. IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3ea0f4f e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"3ea0f4f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-27a8db1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"27a8db1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The International Residential Code (IRC) sets safety and design standards for stairways in residential buildings, ensuring they meet structural, accessibility, and usability requirements. These guidelines help prevent accidents and improve comfort in homes.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IRC Stairway Regulations:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Maximum Riser Height<\\/strong>: Defines the height of each step to maintain consistency and ease of movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Minimum Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Ensures sufficient foot space for stability while ascending or descending.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1d689e0 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"1d689e0\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3428 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" width=\\\"1024\\\" height=\\\"590\\\"><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f5666db e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"f5666db\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3780e4a elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"3780e4a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Handrail Requirements<\\/strong>: Specifies height and graspability for added safety and support.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Guardrail Standards<\\/strong>: Prevents falls by establishing minimum railing height and spacing.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing Dimensions<\\/strong>: Regulates the size and placement of stair landings for safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Headroom Clearance<\\/strong>: Ensures adequate overhead space to prevent obstructions.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>These IRC rules play a crucial role in designing residential stairways that are both functional and compliant with safety standards.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ce18657 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ce18657\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-adc4321 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"adc4321\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">3. OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-55edcc6 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"55edcc6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-56630d5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"56630d5\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) is a U.S. government agency responsible for ensuring safe and healthy working conditions. Established in 1970 under the Occupational Safety and Health Act, OSHA sets regulations and conducts inspections to protect workers across various industries.<\\/p>\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) standard 1910.25 outlines safety requirements for stairways in workplaces to prevent accidents and ensure structural integrity. These regulations apply to various stair types, including standard, spiral, ship, and alternating tread stairs.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-10bffc2 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"10bffc2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3432 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\"><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ada56dd e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ada56dd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fd0407a e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"fd0407a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0f39eee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"0f39eee\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default elementor-inline-editing pen\\\" spellcheck=\\\"false\\\" data-elementor-setting-key=\\\"title\\\" data-pen-placeholder=\\\"Type Here...\\\" data-qb-tmp-id=\\\"lt-738382\\\" data-gramm=\\\"false\\\" contenteditable=\\\"true\\\">4. ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/h5>\\n<p>The Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) establishes accessibility standards for stairways to ensure safe and inclusive navigation for individuals with disabilities. These regulations apply to both interior and exterior stairs in public buildings and facilities.<br>Key ADA Stairway Requirements:<br><strong>Uniform Step Dimensions<\\/strong>: All steps must have consistent depth and height to prevent tripping hazards.<br><strong>Step Height<\\/strong>: Must be between 5 and 7 inches for accessibility.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Minimum of 11 inches, measured from riser to riser, to provide secure footing.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Stair Width<\\/strong>: Must be at least 36 inches to accommodate users safely.<br><strong>Handrails<\\/strong>: Required on both sides of stairways, positioned 34 to 38 inches above the stair nosing.<br><strong>Nosings<\\/strong>: Must not project more than 1.5 inches beyond the riser below to reduce tripping risks.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-8baa50f elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"8baa50f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><br><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-bbd2929 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"bbd2929\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c40a9f7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"c40a9f7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3469 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\"><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0c64e0e elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"0c64e0e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3465 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\"><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-57c9bd3 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"57c9bd3\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3477 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\"><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-e411696 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"e411696\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2fada2e elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"2fada2e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">5. PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2e1c457 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"2e1c457\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>PIP Civil, Structural, and Architectural (CSA) Practices publishes essential CSA Engineering Design Practices, including specifications and fabrication\\/installation details.<\\/p>\\n<p>This Practice provides fabrication and installation details for standard pipe railing for walking and working surfaces and for stair railing or handrail for egress. Although the details in this practice are intended to meet U.S. Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) requirements for process facilities, they may not meet the requirements of local or national building codes.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-82239ba e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"82239ba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-125261c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"125261c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section4\\\">4. CONCLUSION<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>Building codes for stairs are established to enhance safety for all users, including children, the elderly, and individuals with disabilities.<\\/p>\\n<p>They help minimize the risks of slips, trips, and falls while ensuring uniformity in design and construction for both contractors and homeowners.<\\/p>\\n<p>The codes outlined above play a crucial role in stair design and construction, with periodic updates to accommodate evolving safety standards and requirements.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1247,795,'_wp_page_template','default'),(1248,795,'_thumbnail_id','1133'),(1249,795,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1250,795,'_elementor_template_type','wp-post'),(1251,795,'_elementor_version','3.28.4'),(1252,795,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"3415c006\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":[],\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"542b4229\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"editor\":\"<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-644be11 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"644be11\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\" data-settings=\\\"{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c134fba elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"c134fba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>Stairs play a crucial role in architecture, offering vertical connectivity between floors in multi-story buildings while fulfilling a functional purpose. Stairs are a structure that allows movement between different levels by dividing the vertical distance into smaller, manageable steps.<\\/p>\\n<p>Stairs encompass staircases, also called stairways, as well as escalators. Alternatives to traditional stairs include elevators (lifts), stair lifts, inclined moving walkways, ladders, and ramps.<\\/p>\\n<p>This article aims to highlight key aspects of stair codes relevant to steel detailing.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1ce422f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"1ce422f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f159939 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"f159939\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2>Table of Contents<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-5e86856 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-mobile__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"5e86856\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section1\\\">Introduction<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section2\\\">Stair Codes and Their Significance <\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section3\\\">Codes and Standards Applicable to Steel Detailing<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section4\\\">Conclusion<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3126a5f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"3126a5f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b99b920 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"b99b920\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section1\\\">1. INTRODUCTION<\\/h2>\\n<div>Stair codes play a vital role in safety, ensuring that stairs are designed to minimize the risk of falls and injuries. These regulations dictate key dimensions such as tread depth, riser height, and handrail specifications, all enforced to safeguard users.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d3ea5c7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"d3ea5c7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section2\\\">2. STAIR CODES AND THEIR IMPORTANCE<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>In the United States, stair detailing must adhere to various codes and standards to ensure safety, accessibility, and structural integrity. These regulations define essential aspects such as tread depth, riser height, handrails, and load-bearing requirements.<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Code Council was established in 1994, with the goal of developing a single set of national model construction codes. It brought together three different organizations that had developed three separate sets of model codes throughout the U.S.: Building Offi\\u00adcials and Code Administrators International, Inc. (BOCA), International Conference of Building Officials (ICBO) and Southern Building Code Congress International, Inc. (SBCCI).<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Building Code (IBC) and International Residential Code (IRC) are model building codes developed by the International Code Council (ICC) that are adopted by many jurisdictions in the US to ensure public safety and welfare in the built environment. The IBC applies to most structures, while the IRC specifically addresses one- and two-family dwellings.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-51aa218 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"51aa218\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section3\\\">3. CODES AND STANDARDS USED IN STEEL DETAILING<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>The following codes are applied in stair detailing:<\\/p>\\n<ol>\\n<li>IBC (International Building Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/li>\\n<li>ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/li>\\n<li>PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d1ec165 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d1ec165\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a49f34d e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"a49f34d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-88bd7bd elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"88bd7bd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5><strong>1. IBC (International Building Code)<\\/strong><\\/h5>\\n<p>The IBC is a model building code that provides a comprehensive set of guidelines for the design, construction, and safety of buildings, with the goal of protecting public health, safety, and welfare.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IBC Requirements for Stairways:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Width and Clearance<\\/strong>: Defines minimum stairway width for safe passage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Tread and Riser Dimensions<\\/strong>: Specifies uniform riser heights and tread depths for comfortable and secure movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Handrails and Guardrails<\\/strong>: Sets rules for placement, height, and design to enhance stability and prevent falls.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing and Platforms<\\/strong>: Regulates landing dimensions to provide resting points and safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Fire Safety and Egress<\\/strong>: Ensures stairways support emergency evacuation routes with proper fire-resistant materials and signage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Accessibility Compliance<\\/strong>: Aligns with ADA guidelines to accommodate users with mobility challenges.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ece6749 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"ece6749\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3421 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"AISC - Design_Guide - STAIR MINIMUM REQUIREMENT SKETCH\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\"><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d20752c e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d20752c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-97c617a elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"97c617a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">2. IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3ea0f4f e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"3ea0f4f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-27a8db1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"27a8db1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The International Residential Code (IRC) sets safety and design standards for stairways in residential buildings, ensuring they meet structural, accessibility, and usability requirements. These guidelines help prevent accidents and improve comfort in homes.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IRC Stairway Regulations:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Maximum Riser Height<\\/strong>: Defines the height of each step to maintain consistency and ease of movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Minimum Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Ensures sufficient foot space for stability while ascending or descending.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1d689e0 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"1d689e0\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3428 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" width=\\\"1024\\\" height=\\\"590\\\"><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f5666db e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"f5666db\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3780e4a elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"3780e4a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Handrail Requirements<\\/strong>: Specifies height and graspability for added safety and support.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Guardrail Standards<\\/strong>: Prevents falls by establishing minimum railing height and spacing.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing Dimensions<\\/strong>: Regulates the size and placement of stair landings for safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Headroom Clearance<\\/strong>: Ensures adequate overhead space to prevent obstructions.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>These IRC rules play a crucial role in designing residential stairways that are both functional and compliant with safety standards.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ce18657 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ce18657\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-adc4321 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"adc4321\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">3. OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-55edcc6 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"55edcc6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-56630d5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"56630d5\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) is a U.S. government agency responsible for ensuring safe and healthy working conditions. Established in 1970 under the Occupational Safety and Health Act, OSHA sets regulations and conducts inspections to protect workers across various industries.<\\/p>\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) standard 1910.25 outlines safety requirements for stairways in workplaces to prevent accidents and ensure structural integrity. These regulations apply to various stair types, including standard, spiral, ship, and alternating tread stairs.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-10bffc2 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"10bffc2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3432 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\"><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ada56dd e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ada56dd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fd0407a e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"fd0407a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0f39eee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"0f39eee\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default elementor-inline-editing pen\\\" spellcheck=\\\"false\\\" data-elementor-setting-key=\\\"title\\\" data-pen-placeholder=\\\"Type Here...\\\" data-qb-tmp-id=\\\"lt-738382\\\" data-gramm=\\\"false\\\" contenteditable=\\\"true\\\">4. ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/h5>\\n<p>The Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) establishes accessibility standards for stairways to ensure safe and inclusive navigation for individuals with disabilities. These regulations apply to both interior and exterior stairs in public buildings and facilities.<br>Key ADA Stairway Requirements:<br><strong>Uniform Step Dimensions<\\/strong>: All steps must have consistent depth and height to prevent tripping hazards.<br><strong>Step Height<\\/strong>: Must be between 5 and 7 inches for accessibility.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Minimum of 11 inches, measured from riser to riser, to provide secure footing.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Stair Width<\\/strong>: Must be at least 36 inches to accommodate users safely.<br><strong>Handrails<\\/strong>: Required on both sides of stairways, positioned 34 to 38 inches above the stair nosing.<br><strong>Nosings<\\/strong>: Must not project more than 1.5 inches beyond the riser below to reduce tripping risks.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-8baa50f elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"8baa50f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><br><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-bbd2929 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"bbd2929\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c40a9f7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"c40a9f7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3469 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\"><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0c64e0e elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"0c64e0e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3465 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\"><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-57c9bd3 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"57c9bd3\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3477 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\"><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-e411696 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"e411696\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2fada2e elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"2fada2e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">5. PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2e1c457 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"2e1c457\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>PIP Civil, Structural, and Architectural (CSA) Practices publishes essential CSA Engineering Design Practices, including specifications and fabrication\\/installation details.<\\/p>\\n<p>This Practice provides fabrication and installation details for standard pipe railing for walking and working surfaces and for stair railing or handrail for egress. Although the details in this practice are intended to meet U.S. Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) requirements for process facilities, they may not meet the requirements of local or national building codes.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-82239ba e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"82239ba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-125261c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"125261c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section4\\\">4. CONCLUSION<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>Building codes for stairs are established to enhance safety for all users, including children, the elderly, and individuals with disabilities.<\\/p>\\n<p>They help minimize the risks of slips, trips, and falls while ensuring uniformity in design and construction for both contractors and homeowners.<\\/p>\\n<p>The codes outlined above play a crucial role in stair design and construction, with periodic updates to accommodate evolving safety standards and requirements.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1254,796,'_wp_page_template','default'),(1255,796,'_thumbnail_id','1133'),(1256,796,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1257,796,'_elementor_template_type','wp-post'),(1258,796,'_elementor_version','3.28.4'),(1259,796,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"3415c006\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":[],\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"542b4229\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"editor\":\"<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-644be11 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"644be11\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\" data-settings=\\\"{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c134fba elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"c134fba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>Stairs play a crucial role in architecture, offering vertical connectivity between floors in multi-story buildings while fulfilling a functional purpose. Stairs are a structure that allows movement between different levels by dividing the vertical distance into smaller, manageable steps.<\\/p>\\n<p>Stairs encompass staircases, also called stairways, as well as escalators. Alternatives to traditional stairs include elevators (lifts), stair lifts, inclined moving walkways, ladders, and ramps.<\\/p>\\n<p>This article aims to highlight key aspects of stair codes relevant to steel detailing.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1ce422f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"1ce422f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f159939 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"f159939\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2>Table of Contents<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-5e86856 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-mobile__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"5e86856\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section1\\\">Introduction<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section2\\\">Stair Codes and Their Significance <\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section3\\\">Codes and Standards Applicable to Steel Detailing<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section4\\\">Conclusion<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3126a5f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"3126a5f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b99b920 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"b99b920\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section1\\\">1. INTRODUCTION<\\/h2>\\n<div>Stair codes play a vital role in safety, ensuring that stairs are designed to minimize the risk of falls and injuries. These regulations dictate key dimensions such as tread depth, riser height, and handrail specifications, all enforced to safeguard users.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d3ea5c7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"d3ea5c7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section2\\\">2. STAIR CODES AND THEIR IMPORTANCE<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>In the United States, stair detailing must adhere to various codes and standards to ensure safety, accessibility, and structural integrity. These regulations define essential aspects such as tread depth, riser height, handrails, and load-bearing requirements.<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Code Council was established in 1994, with the goal of developing a single set of national model construction codes. It brought together three different organizations that had developed three separate sets of model codes throughout the U.S.: Building Offi\\u00adcials and Code Administrators International, Inc. (BOCA), International Conference of Building Officials (ICBO) and Southern Building Code Congress International, Inc. (SBCCI).<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Building Code (IBC) and International Residential Code (IRC) are model building codes developed by the International Code Council (ICC) that are adopted by many jurisdictions in the US to ensure public safety and welfare in the built environment. The IBC applies to most structures, while the IRC specifically addresses one- and two-family dwellings.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-51aa218 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"51aa218\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section3\\\">3. CODES AND STANDARDS USED IN STEEL DETAILING<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>The following codes are applied in stair detailing:<\\/p>\\n<ol>\\n<li>IBC (International Building Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/li>\\n<li>ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/li>\\n<li>PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d1ec165 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d1ec165\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a49f34d e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"a49f34d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-88bd7bd elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"88bd7bd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5><strong>1. IBC (International Building Code)<\\/strong><\\/h5>\\n<p>The IBC is a model building code that provides a comprehensive set of guidelines for the design, construction, and safety of buildings, with the goal of protecting public health, safety, and welfare.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IBC Requirements for Stairways:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Width and Clearance<\\/strong>: Defines minimum stairway width for safe passage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Tread and Riser Dimensions<\\/strong>: Specifies uniform riser heights and tread depths for comfortable and secure movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Handrails and Guardrails<\\/strong>: Sets rules for placement, height, and design to enhance stability and prevent falls.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing and Platforms<\\/strong>: Regulates landing dimensions to provide resting points and safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Fire Safety and Egress<\\/strong>: Ensures stairways support emergency evacuation routes with proper fire-resistant materials and signage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Accessibility Compliance<\\/strong>: Aligns with ADA guidelines to accommodate users with mobility challenges.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ece6749 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"ece6749\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3421 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"AISC - Design_Guide - STAIR MINIMUM REQUIREMENT SKETCH\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d20752c e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d20752c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-97c617a elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"97c617a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">2. IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3ea0f4f e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"3ea0f4f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-27a8db1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"27a8db1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The International Residential Code (IRC) sets safety and design standards for stairways in residential buildings, ensuring they meet structural, accessibility, and usability requirements. These guidelines help prevent accidents and improve comfort in homes.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IRC Stairway Regulations:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Maximum Riser Height<\\/strong>: Defines the height of each step to maintain consistency and ease of movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Minimum Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Ensures sufficient foot space for stability while ascending or descending.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1d689e0 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"1d689e0\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3428 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"1024\\\" height=\\\"590\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f5666db e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"f5666db\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3780e4a elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"3780e4a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Handrail Requirements<\\/strong>: Specifies height and graspability for added safety and support.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Guardrail Standards<\\/strong>: Prevents falls by establishing minimum railing height and spacing.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing Dimensions<\\/strong>: Regulates the size and placement of stair landings for safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Headroom Clearance<\\/strong>: Ensures adequate overhead space to prevent obstructions.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>These IRC rules play a crucial role in designing residential stairways that are both functional and compliant with safety standards.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ce18657 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ce18657\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-adc4321 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"adc4321\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">3. OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-55edcc6 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"55edcc6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-56630d5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"56630d5\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) is a U.S. government agency responsible for ensuring safe and healthy working conditions. Established in 1970 under the Occupational Safety and Health Act, OSHA sets regulations and conducts inspections to protect workers across various industries.<\\/p>\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) standard 1910.25 outlines safety requirements for stairways in workplaces to prevent accidents and ensure structural integrity. These regulations apply to various stair types, including standard, spiral, ship, and alternating tread stairs.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-10bffc2 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"10bffc2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3432 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ada56dd e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ada56dd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fd0407a e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"fd0407a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0f39eee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"0f39eee\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default elementor-inline-editing pen\\\" contenteditable=\\\"true\\\" spellcheck=\\\"false\\\" data-elementor-setting-key=\\\"title\\\" data-pen-placeholder=\\\"Type Here...\\\" data-qb-tmp-id=\\\"lt-738382\\\" data-gramm=\\\"false\\\">4. ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/h5>\\n<p>The Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) establishes accessibility standards for stairways to ensure safe and inclusive navigation for individuals with disabilities. These regulations apply to both interior and exterior stairs in public buildings and facilities.<br \\/>Key ADA Stairway Requirements:<br \\/><strong>Uniform Step Dimensions<\\/strong>: All steps must have consistent depth and height to prevent tripping hazards.<br \\/><strong>Step Height<\\/strong>: Must be between 5 and 7 inches for accessibility.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Minimum of 11 inches, measured from riser to riser, to provide secure footing.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Stair Width<\\/strong>: Must be at least 36 inches to accommodate users safely.<br \\/><strong>Handrails<\\/strong>: Required on both sides of stairways, positioned 34 to 38 inches above the stair nosing.<br \\/><strong>Nosings<\\/strong>: Must not project more than 1.5 inches beyond the riser below to reduce tripping risks.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-8baa50f elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"8baa50f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\u00a0<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-bbd2929 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"bbd2929\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c40a9f7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"c40a9f7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3469 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0c64e0e elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"0c64e0e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3465 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-57c9bd3 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"57c9bd3\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3477 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-e411696 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"e411696\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2fada2e elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"2fada2e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">5. PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2e1c457 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"2e1c457\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>PIP Civil, Structural, and Architectural (CSA) Practices publishes essential CSA Engineering Design Practices, including specifications and fabrication\\/installation details.<\\/p>\\n<p>This Practice provides fabrication and installation details for standard pipe railing for walking and working surfaces and for stair railing or handrail for egress. Although the details in this practice are intended to meet U.S. Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) requirements for process facilities, they may not meet the requirements of local or national building codes.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-82239ba e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"82239ba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-125261c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"125261c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section4\\\">4. CONCLUSION<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>Building codes for stairs are established to enhance safety for all users, including children, the elderly, and individuals with disabilities.<\\/p>\\n<p>They help minimize the risks of slips, trips, and falls while ensuring uniformity in design and construction for both contractors and homeowners.<\\/p>\\n<p>The codes outlined above play a crucial role in stair design and construction, with periodic updates to accommodate evolving safety standards and requirements.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1261,797,'_wp_page_template','default'),(1262,797,'_thumbnail_id','1133'),(1263,797,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1264,797,'_elementor_template_type','wp-post'),(1265,797,'_elementor_version','3.28.4'),(1266,797,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"3415c006\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":[],\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"542b4229\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"editor\":\"<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-644be11 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"644be11\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\" data-settings=\\\"{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c134fba elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"c134fba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>Stairs play a crucial role in architecture, offering vertical connectivity between floors in multi-story buildings while fulfilling a functional purpose. Stairs are a structure that allows movement between different levels by dividing the vertical distance into smaller, manageable steps.<\\/p>\\n<p>Stairs encompass staircases, also called stairways, as well as escalators. Alternatives to traditional stairs include elevators (lifts), stair lifts, inclined moving walkways, ladders, and ramps.<\\/p>\\n<p>This article aims to highlight key aspects of stair codes relevant to steel detailing.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1ce422f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"1ce422f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f159939 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"f159939\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2>Table of Contents<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-5e86856 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-mobile__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"5e86856\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section1\\\">Introduction<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section2\\\">Stair Codes and Their Significance <\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section3\\\">Codes and Standards Applicable to Steel Detailing<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section4\\\">Conclusion<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3126a5f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"3126a5f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b99b920 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"b99b920\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section1\\\">1. INTRODUCTION<\\/h2>\\n<div>Stair codes play a vital role in safety, ensuring that stairs are designed to minimize the risk of falls and injuries. These regulations dictate key dimensions such as tread depth, riser height, and handrail specifications, all enforced to safeguard users.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d3ea5c7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"d3ea5c7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section2\\\">2. STAIR CODES AND THEIR IMPORTANCE<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>In the United States, stair detailing must adhere to various codes and standards to ensure safety, accessibility, and structural integrity. These regulations define essential aspects such as tread depth, riser height, handrails, and load-bearing requirements.<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Code Council was established in 1994, with the goal of developing a single set of national model construction codes. It brought together three different organizations that had developed three separate sets of model codes throughout the U.S.: Building Offi\\u00adcials and Code Administrators International, Inc. (BOCA), International Conference of Building Officials (ICBO) and Southern Building Code Congress International, Inc. (SBCCI).<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Building Code (IBC) and International Residential Code (IRC) are model building codes developed by the International Code Council (ICC) that are adopted by many jurisdictions in the US to ensure public safety and welfare in the built environment. The IBC applies to most structures, while the IRC specifically addresses one- and two-family dwellings.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-51aa218 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"51aa218\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section3\\\">3. CODES AND STANDARDS USED IN STEEL DETAILING<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>The following codes are applied in stair detailing:<\\/p>\\n<ol>\\n<li>IBC (International Building Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/li>\\n<li>ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/li>\\n<li>PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d1ec165 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d1ec165\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a49f34d e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"a49f34d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-88bd7bd elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"88bd7bd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5><strong>1. IBC (International Building Code)<\\/strong><\\/h5>\\n<p>The IBC is a model building code that provides a comprehensive set of guidelines for the design, construction, and safety of buildings, with the goal of protecting public health, safety, and welfare.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IBC Requirements for Stairways:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Width and Clearance<\\/strong>: Defines minimum stairway width for safe passage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Tread and Riser Dimensions<\\/strong>: Specifies uniform riser heights and tread depths for comfortable and secure movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Handrails and Guardrails<\\/strong>: Sets rules for placement, height, and design to enhance stability and prevent falls.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing and Platforms<\\/strong>: Regulates landing dimensions to provide resting points and safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Fire Safety and Egress<\\/strong>: Ensures stairways support emergency evacuation routes with proper fire-resistant materials and signage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Accessibility Compliance<\\/strong>: Aligns with ADA guidelines to accommodate users with mobility challenges.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ece6749 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"ece6749\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3421 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"AISC - Design_Guide - STAIR MINIMUM REQUIREMENT SKETCH\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d20752c e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d20752c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-97c617a elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"97c617a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">2. IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3ea0f4f e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"3ea0f4f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-27a8db1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"27a8db1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The International Residential Code (IRC) sets safety and design standards for stairways in residential buildings, ensuring they meet structural, accessibility, and usability requirements. These guidelines help prevent accidents and improve comfort in homes.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IRC Stairway Regulations:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Maximum Riser Height<\\/strong>: Defines the height of each step to maintain consistency and ease of movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Minimum Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Ensures sufficient foot space for stability while ascending or descending.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1d689e0 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"1d689e0\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3428 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"1024\\\" height=\\\"590\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f5666db e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"f5666db\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3780e4a elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"3780e4a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Handrail Requirements<\\/strong>: Specifies height and graspability for added safety and support.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Guardrail Standards<\\/strong>: Prevents falls by establishing minimum railing height and spacing.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing Dimensions<\\/strong>: Regulates the size and placement of stair landings for safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Headroom Clearance<\\/strong>: Ensures adequate overhead space to prevent obstructions.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>These IRC rules play a crucial role in designing residential stairways that are both functional and compliant with safety standards.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ce18657 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ce18657\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-adc4321 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"adc4321\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">3. OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-55edcc6 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"55edcc6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-56630d5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"56630d5\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) is a U.S. government agency responsible for ensuring safe and healthy working conditions. Established in 1970 under the Occupational Safety and Health Act, OSHA sets regulations and conducts inspections to protect workers across various industries.<\\/p>\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) standard 1910.25 outlines safety requirements for stairways in workplaces to prevent accidents and ensure structural integrity. These regulations apply to various stair types, including standard, spiral, ship, and alternating tread stairs.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-10bffc2 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"10bffc2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3432 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ada56dd e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ada56dd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fd0407a e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"fd0407a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0f39eee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"0f39eee\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default elementor-inline-editing pen\\\" contenteditable=\\\"true\\\" spellcheck=\\\"false\\\" data-elementor-setting-key=\\\"title\\\" data-pen-placeholder=\\\"Type Here...\\\" data-qb-tmp-id=\\\"lt-738382\\\" data-gramm=\\\"false\\\">4. ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/h5>\\n<p>The Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) establishes accessibility standards for stairways to ensure safe and inclusive navigation for individuals with disabilities. These regulations apply to both interior and exterior stairs in public buildings and facilities.<br \\/>Key ADA Stairway Requirements:<br \\/><strong>Uniform Step Dimensions<\\/strong>: All steps must have consistent depth and height to prevent tripping hazards.<br \\/><strong>Step Height<\\/strong>: Must be between 5 and 7 inches for accessibility.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Minimum of 11 inches, measured from riser to riser, to provide secure footing.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Stair Width<\\/strong>: Must be at least 36 inches to accommodate users safely.<br \\/><strong>Handrails<\\/strong>: Required on both sides of stairways, positioned 34 to 38 inches above the stair nosing.<br \\/><strong>Nosings<\\/strong>: Must not project more than 1.5 inches beyond the riser below to reduce tripping risks.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-8baa50f elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"8baa50f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\u00a0<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-bbd2929 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"bbd2929\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c40a9f7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"c40a9f7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3469 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0c64e0e elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"0c64e0e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3465 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-57c9bd3 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"57c9bd3\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3477 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-e411696 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"e411696\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2fada2e elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"2fada2e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">5. PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2e1c457 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"2e1c457\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>PIP Civil, Structural, and Architectural (CSA) Practices publishes essential CSA Engineering Design Practices, including specifications and fabrication\\/installation details.<\\/p>\\n<p>This Practice provides fabrication and installation details for standard pipe railing for walking and working surfaces and for stair railing or handrail for egress. Although the details in this practice are intended to meet U.S. Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) requirements for process facilities, they may not meet the requirements of local or national building codes.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-82239ba e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"82239ba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-125261c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"125261c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section4\\\">4. CONCLUSION<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>Building codes for stairs are established to enhance safety for all users, including children, the elderly, and individuals with disabilities.<\\/p>\\n<p>They help minimize the risks of slips, trips, and falls while ensuring uniformity in design and construction for both contractors and homeowners.<\\/p>\\n<p>The codes outlined above play a crucial role in stair design and construction, with periodic updates to accommodate evolving safety standards and requirements.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1268,798,'_wp_attached_file','2025/05/weslider-5.jpg'),(1269,798,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:275;s:6:\"height\";i:183;s:4:\"file\";s:22:\"2025/05/weslider-5.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:12001;s:5:\"sizes\";a:2:{s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:22:\"weslider-5-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:8156;}s:11:\"total-thumb\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:22:\"weslider-5-100x100.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:100;s:6:\"height\";i:100;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:3943;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:12:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"0\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}}}'),(1270,799,'_wp_page_template','default'),(1271,799,'_thumbnail_id','1133'),(1272,799,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1273,799,'_elementor_template_type','wp-post'),(1274,799,'_elementor_version','3.28.4'),(1275,799,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"3415c006\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":[],\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"542b4229\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"editor\":\"<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-644be11 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"644be11\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\" data-settings=\\\"{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c134fba elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"c134fba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>Stairs play a crucial role in architecture, offering vertical connectivity between floors in multi-story buildings while fulfilling a functional purpose. Stairs are a structure that allows movement between different levels by dividing the vertical distance into smaller, manageable steps.<\\/p>\\n<p>Stairs encompass staircases, also called stairways, as well as escalators. Alternatives to traditional stairs include elevators (lifts), stair lifts, inclined moving walkways, ladders, and ramps.<\\/p>\\n<p>This article aims to highlight key aspects of stair codes relevant to steel detailing.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1ce422f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"1ce422f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f159939 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"f159939\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2>Table of Contents<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-5e86856 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-mobile__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"5e86856\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section1\\\">Introduction<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section2\\\">Stair Codes and Their Significance <\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section3\\\">Codes and Standards Applicable to Steel Detailing<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section4\\\">Conclusion<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3126a5f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"3126a5f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b99b920 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"b99b920\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section1\\\">1. INTRODUCTION<\\/h2>\\n<div>Stair codes play a vital role in safety, ensuring that stairs are designed to minimize the risk of falls and injuries. These regulations dictate key dimensions such as tread depth, riser height, and handrail specifications, all enforced to safeguard users.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d3ea5c7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"d3ea5c7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section2\\\">2. STAIR CODES AND THEIR IMPORTANCE<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>In the United States, stair detailing must adhere to various codes and standards to ensure safety, accessibility, and structural integrity. These regulations define essential aspects such as tread depth, riser height, handrails, and load-bearing requirements.<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Code Council was established in 1994, with the goal of developing a single set of national model construction codes. It brought together three different organizations that had developed three separate sets of model codes throughout the U.S.: Building Offi\\u00adcials and Code Administrators International, Inc. (BOCA), International Conference of Building Officials (ICBO) and Southern Building Code Congress International, Inc. (SBCCI).<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Building Code (IBC) and International Residential Code (IRC) are model building codes developed by the International Code Council (ICC) that are adopted by many jurisdictions in the US to ensure public safety and welfare in the built environment. The IBC applies to most structures, while the IRC specifically addresses one- and two-family dwellings.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-51aa218 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"51aa218\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section3\\\">3. CODES AND STANDARDS USED IN STEEL DETAILING<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>The following codes are applied in stair detailing:<\\/p>\\n<ol>\\n<li>IBC (International Building Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/li>\\n<li>ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/li>\\n<li>PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d1ec165 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d1ec165\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a49f34d e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"a49f34d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-88bd7bd elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"88bd7bd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5><strong>1. IBC (International Building Code)<\\/strong><\\/h5>\\n<p>The IBC is a model building code that provides a comprehensive set of guidelines for the design, construction, and safety of buildings, with the goal of protecting public health, safety, and welfare.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IBC Requirements for Stairways:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Width and Clearance<\\/strong>: Defines minimum stairway width for safe passage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Tread and Riser Dimensions<\\/strong>: Specifies uniform riser heights and tread depths for comfortable and secure movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Handrails and Guardrails<\\/strong>: Sets rules for placement, height, and design to enhance stability and prevent falls.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing and Platforms<\\/strong>: Regulates landing dimensions to provide resting points and safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Fire Safety and Egress<\\/strong>: Ensures stairways support emergency evacuation routes with proper fire-resistant materials and signage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Accessibility Compliance<\\/strong>: Aligns with ADA guidelines to accommodate users with mobility challenges.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ece6749 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"ece6749\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3421 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"AISC - Design_Guide - STAIR MINIMUM REQUIREMENT SKETCH\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d20752c e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d20752c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-97c617a elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"97c617a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">2. IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3ea0f4f e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"3ea0f4f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-27a8db1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"27a8db1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The International Residential Code (IRC) sets safety and design standards for stairways in residential buildings, ensuring they meet structural, accessibility, and usability requirements. These guidelines help prevent accidents and improve comfort in homes.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IRC Stairway Regulations:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Maximum Riser Height<\\/strong>: Defines the height of each step to maintain consistency and ease of movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Minimum Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Ensures sufficient foot space for stability while ascending or descending.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1d689e0 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"1d689e0\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3428 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"1024\\\" height=\\\"590\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f5666db e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"f5666db\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3780e4a elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"3780e4a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Handrail Requirements<\\/strong>: Specifies height and graspability for added safety and support.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Guardrail Standards<\\/strong>: Prevents falls by establishing minimum railing height and spacing.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing Dimensions<\\/strong>: Regulates the size and placement of stair landings for safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Headroom Clearance<\\/strong>: Ensures adequate overhead space to prevent obstructions.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>These IRC rules play a crucial role in designing residential stairways that are both functional and compliant with safety standards.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ce18657 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ce18657\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-adc4321 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"adc4321\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">3. OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-55edcc6 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"55edcc6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-56630d5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"56630d5\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) is a U.S. government agency responsible for ensuring safe and healthy working conditions. Established in 1970 under the Occupational Safety and Health Act, OSHA sets regulations and conducts inspections to protect workers across various industries.<\\/p>\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) standard 1910.25 outlines safety requirements for stairways in workplaces to prevent accidents and ensure structural integrity. These regulations apply to various stair types, including standard, spiral, ship, and alternating tread stairs.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-10bffc2 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"10bffc2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3432 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ada56dd e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ada56dd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fd0407a e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"fd0407a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0f39eee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"0f39eee\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default elementor-inline-editing pen\\\" contenteditable=\\\"true\\\" spellcheck=\\\"false\\\" data-elementor-setting-key=\\\"title\\\" data-pen-placeholder=\\\"Type Here...\\\" data-qb-tmp-id=\\\"lt-738382\\\" data-gramm=\\\"false\\\">4. ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/h5>\\n<p>The Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) establishes accessibility standards for stairways to ensure safe and inclusive navigation for individuals with disabilities. These regulations apply to both interior and exterior stairs in public buildings and facilities.<br \\/>Key ADA Stairway Requirements:<br \\/><strong>Uniform Step Dimensions<\\/strong>: All steps must have consistent depth and height to prevent tripping hazards.<br \\/><strong>Step Height<\\/strong>: Must be between 5 and 7 inches for accessibility.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Minimum of 11 inches, measured from riser to riser, to provide secure footing.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Stair Width<\\/strong>: Must be at least 36 inches to accommodate users safely.<br \\/><strong>Handrails<\\/strong>: Required on both sides of stairways, positioned 34 to 38 inches above the stair nosing.<br \\/><strong>Nosings<\\/strong>: Must not project more than 1.5 inches beyond the riser below to reduce tripping risks.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-8baa50f elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"8baa50f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\u00a0<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-bbd2929 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"bbd2929\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c40a9f7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"c40a9f7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3469 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0c64e0e elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"0c64e0e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3465 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-57c9bd3 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"57c9bd3\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3477 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-e411696 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"e411696\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2fada2e elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"2fada2e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">5. PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2e1c457 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"2e1c457\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>PIP Civil, Structural, and Architectural (CSA) Practices publishes essential CSA Engineering Design Practices, including specifications and fabrication\\/installation details.<\\/p>\\n<p>This Practice provides fabrication and installation details for standard pipe railing for walking and working surfaces and for stair railing or handrail for egress. Although the details in this practice are intended to meet U.S. Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) requirements for process facilities, they may not meet the requirements of local or national building codes.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-82239ba e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"82239ba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-125261c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"125261c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section4\\\">4. CONCLUSION<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>Building codes for stairs are established to enhance safety for all users, including children, the elderly, and individuals with disabilities.<\\/p>\\n<p>They help minimize the risks of slips, trips, and falls while ensuring uniformity in design and construction for both contractors and homeowners.<\\/p>\\n<p>The codes outlined above play a crucial role in stair design and construction, with periodic updates to accommodate evolving safety standards and requirements.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1277,800,'_wp_page_template','default'),(1278,800,'_thumbnail_id','1133'),(1279,800,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1280,800,'_elementor_template_type','wp-post'),(1281,800,'_elementor_version','3.28.4'),(1282,800,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"3415c006\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":[],\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"542b4229\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"editor\":\"<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-644be11 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"644be11\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\" data-settings=\\\"{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c134fba elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"c134fba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>Stairs play a crucial role in architecture, offering vertical connectivity between floors in multi-story buildings while fulfilling a functional purpose. Stairs are a structure that allows movement between different levels by dividing the vertical distance into smaller, manageable steps.<\\/p>\\n<p>Stairs encompass staircases, also called stairways, as well as escalators. Alternatives to traditional stairs include elevators (lifts), stair lifts, inclined moving walkways, ladders, and ramps.<\\/p>\\n<p>This article aims to highlight key aspects of stair codes relevant to steel detailing.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1ce422f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"1ce422f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f159939 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"f159939\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2>Table of Contents<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-5e86856 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-mobile__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"5e86856\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section1\\\">Introduction<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section2\\\">Stair Codes and Their Significance <\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section3\\\">Codes and Standards Applicable to Steel Detailing<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section4\\\">Conclusion<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3126a5f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"3126a5f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b99b920 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"b99b920\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section1\\\">1. INTRODUCTION<\\/h2>\\n<div>Stair codes play a vital role in safety, ensuring that stairs are designed to minimize the risk of falls and injuries. These regulations dictate key dimensions such as tread depth, riser height, and handrail specifications, all enforced to safeguard users.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d3ea5c7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"d3ea5c7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section2\\\">2. STAIR CODES AND THEIR IMPORTANCE<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>In the United States, stair detailing must adhere to various codes and standards to ensure safety, accessibility, and structural integrity. These regulations define essential aspects such as tread depth, riser height, handrails, and load-bearing requirements.<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Code Council was established in 1994, with the goal of developing a single set of national model construction codes. It brought together three different organizations that had developed three separate sets of model codes throughout the U.S.: Building Offi\\u00adcials and Code Administrators International, Inc. (BOCA), International Conference of Building Officials (ICBO) and Southern Building Code Congress International, Inc. (SBCCI).<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Building Code (IBC) and International Residential Code (IRC) are model building codes developed by the International Code Council (ICC) that are adopted by many jurisdictions in the US to ensure public safety and welfare in the built environment. The IBC applies to most structures, while the IRC specifically addresses one- and two-family dwellings.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-51aa218 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"51aa218\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section3\\\">3. CODES AND STANDARDS USED IN STEEL DETAILING<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>The following codes are applied in stair detailing:<\\/p>\\n<ol>\\n<li>IBC (International Building Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/li>\\n<li>ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/li>\\n<li>PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d1ec165 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d1ec165\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a49f34d e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"a49f34d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-88bd7bd elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"88bd7bd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5><strong>1. IBC (International Building Code)<\\/strong><\\/h5>\\n<p>The IBC is a model building code that provides a comprehensive set of guidelines for the design, construction, and safety of buildings, with the goal of protecting public health, safety, and welfare.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IBC Requirements for Stairways:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Width and Clearance<\\/strong>: Defines minimum stairway width for safe passage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Tread and Riser Dimensions<\\/strong>: Specifies uniform riser heights and tread depths for comfortable and secure movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Handrails and Guardrails<\\/strong>: Sets rules for placement, height, and design to enhance stability and prevent falls.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing and Platforms<\\/strong>: Regulates landing dimensions to provide resting points and safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Fire Safety and Egress<\\/strong>: Ensures stairways support emergency evacuation routes with proper fire-resistant materials and signage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Accessibility Compliance<\\/strong>: Aligns with ADA guidelines to accommodate users with mobility challenges.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ece6749 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"ece6749\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3421 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"AISC - Design_Guide - STAIR MINIMUM REQUIREMENT SKETCH\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d20752c e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d20752c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-97c617a elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"97c617a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">2. IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3ea0f4f e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"3ea0f4f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-27a8db1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"27a8db1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The International Residential Code (IRC) sets safety and design standards for stairways in residential buildings, ensuring they meet structural, accessibility, and usability requirements. These guidelines help prevent accidents and improve comfort in homes.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IRC Stairway Regulations:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Maximum Riser Height<\\/strong>: Defines the height of each step to maintain consistency and ease of movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Minimum Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Ensures sufficient foot space for stability while ascending or descending.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1d689e0 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"1d689e0\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3428 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"1024\\\" height=\\\"590\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f5666db e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"f5666db\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3780e4a elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"3780e4a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Handrail Requirements<\\/strong>: Specifies height and graspability for added safety and support.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Guardrail Standards<\\/strong>: Prevents falls by establishing minimum railing height and spacing.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing Dimensions<\\/strong>: Regulates the size and placement of stair landings for safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Headroom Clearance<\\/strong>: Ensures adequate overhead space to prevent obstructions.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>These IRC rules play a crucial role in designing residential stairways that are both functional and compliant with safety standards.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ce18657 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ce18657\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-adc4321 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"adc4321\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">3. OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-55edcc6 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"55edcc6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-56630d5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"56630d5\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) is a U.S. government agency responsible for ensuring safe and healthy working conditions. Established in 1970 under the Occupational Safety and Health Act, OSHA sets regulations and conducts inspections to protect workers across various industries.<\\/p>\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) standard 1910.25 outlines safety requirements for stairways in workplaces to prevent accidents and ensure structural integrity. These regulations apply to various stair types, including standard, spiral, ship, and alternating tread stairs.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-10bffc2 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"10bffc2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3432 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ada56dd e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ada56dd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fd0407a e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"fd0407a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0f39eee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"0f39eee\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default elementor-inline-editing pen\\\" contenteditable=\\\"true\\\" spellcheck=\\\"false\\\" data-elementor-setting-key=\\\"title\\\" data-pen-placeholder=\\\"Type Here...\\\" data-qb-tmp-id=\\\"lt-738382\\\" data-gramm=\\\"false\\\">4. ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/h5>\\n<p>The Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) establishes accessibility standards for stairways to ensure safe and inclusive navigation for individuals with disabilities. These regulations apply to both interior and exterior stairs in public buildings and facilities.<br \\/>Key ADA Stairway Requirements:<br \\/><strong>Uniform Step Dimensions<\\/strong>: All steps must have consistent depth and height to prevent tripping hazards.<br \\/><strong>Step Height<\\/strong>: Must be between 5 and 7 inches for accessibility.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Minimum of 11 inches, measured from riser to riser, to provide secure footing.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Stair Width<\\/strong>: Must be at least 36 inches to accommodate users safely.<br \\/><strong>Handrails<\\/strong>: Required on both sides of stairways, positioned 34 to 38 inches above the stair nosing.<br \\/><strong>Nosings<\\/strong>: Must not project more than 1.5 inches beyond the riser below to reduce tripping risks.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-8baa50f elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"8baa50f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\u00a0<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-bbd2929 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"bbd2929\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c40a9f7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"c40a9f7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3469 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0c64e0e elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"0c64e0e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3465 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-57c9bd3 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"57c9bd3\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3477 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-e411696 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"e411696\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2fada2e elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"2fada2e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">5. PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2e1c457 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"2e1c457\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>PIP Civil, Structural, and Architectural (CSA) Practices publishes essential CSA Engineering Design Practices, including specifications and fabrication\\/installation details.<\\/p>\\n<p>This Practice provides fabrication and installation details for standard pipe railing for walking and working surfaces and for stair railing or handrail for egress. Although the details in this practice are intended to meet U.S. Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) requirements for process facilities, they may not meet the requirements of local or national building codes.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-82239ba e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"82239ba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-125261c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"125261c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section4\\\">4. CONCLUSION<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>Building codes for stairs are established to enhance safety for all users, including children, the elderly, and individuals with disabilities.<\\/p>\\n<p>They help minimize the risks of slips, trips, and falls while ensuring uniformity in design and construction for both contractors and homeowners.<\\/p>\\n<p>The codes outlined above play a crucial role in stair design and construction, with periodic updates to accommodate evolving safety standards and requirements.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1284,801,'_wp_page_template','default'),(1285,801,'_thumbnail_id','1133'),(1286,801,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1287,801,'_elementor_template_type','wp-post'),(1288,801,'_elementor_version','3.28.4'),(1289,801,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"3415c006\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":{\"background_background\":\"slideshow\"},\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"542b4229\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"editor\":\"<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-644be11 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"644be11\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\" data-settings=\\\"{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c134fba elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"c134fba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>Stairs play a crucial role in architecture, offering vertical connectivity between floors in multi-story buildings while fulfilling a functional purpose. Stairs are a structure that allows movement between different levels by dividing the vertical distance into smaller, manageable steps.<\\/p>\\n<p>Stairs encompass staircases, also called stairways, as well as escalators. Alternatives to traditional stairs include elevators (lifts), stair lifts, inclined moving walkways, ladders, and ramps.<\\/p>\\n<p>This article aims to highlight key aspects of stair codes relevant to steel detailing.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1ce422f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"1ce422f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f159939 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"f159939\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2>Table of Contents<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-5e86856 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-mobile__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"5e86856\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section1\\\">Introduction<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section2\\\">Stair Codes and Their Significance <\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section3\\\">Codes and Standards Applicable to Steel Detailing<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section4\\\">Conclusion<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3126a5f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"3126a5f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b99b920 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"b99b920\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section1\\\">1. INTRODUCTION<\\/h2>\\n<div>Stair codes play a vital role in safety, ensuring that stairs are designed to minimize the risk of falls and injuries. These regulations dictate key dimensions such as tread depth, riser height, and handrail specifications, all enforced to safeguard users.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d3ea5c7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"d3ea5c7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section2\\\">2. STAIR CODES AND THEIR IMPORTANCE<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>In the United States, stair detailing must adhere to various codes and standards to ensure safety, accessibility, and structural integrity. These regulations define essential aspects such as tread depth, riser height, handrails, and load-bearing requirements.<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Code Council was established in 1994, with the goal of developing a single set of national model construction codes. It brought together three different organizations that had developed three separate sets of model codes throughout the U.S.: Building Offi\\u00adcials and Code Administrators International, Inc. (BOCA), International Conference of Building Officials (ICBO) and Southern Building Code Congress International, Inc. (SBCCI).<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Building Code (IBC) and International Residential Code (IRC) are model building codes developed by the International Code Council (ICC) that are adopted by many jurisdictions in the US to ensure public safety and welfare in the built environment. The IBC applies to most structures, while the IRC specifically addresses one- and two-family dwellings.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-51aa218 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"51aa218\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section3\\\">3. CODES AND STANDARDS USED IN STEEL DETAILING<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>The following codes are applied in stair detailing:<\\/p>\\n<ol>\\n<li>IBC (International Building Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/li>\\n<li>ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/li>\\n<li>PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d1ec165 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d1ec165\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a49f34d e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"a49f34d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-88bd7bd elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"88bd7bd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5><strong>1. IBC (International Building Code)<\\/strong><\\/h5>\\n<p>The IBC is a model building code that provides a comprehensive set of guidelines for the design, construction, and safety of buildings, with the goal of protecting public health, safety, and welfare.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IBC Requirements for Stairways:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Width and Clearance<\\/strong>: Defines minimum stairway width for safe passage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Tread and Riser Dimensions<\\/strong>: Specifies uniform riser heights and tread depths for comfortable and secure movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Handrails and Guardrails<\\/strong>: Sets rules for placement, height, and design to enhance stability and prevent falls.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing and Platforms<\\/strong>: Regulates landing dimensions to provide resting points and safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Fire Safety and Egress<\\/strong>: Ensures stairways support emergency evacuation routes with proper fire-resistant materials and signage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Accessibility Compliance<\\/strong>: Aligns with ADA guidelines to accommodate users with mobility challenges.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ece6749 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"ece6749\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3421 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"AISC - Design_Guide - STAIR MINIMUM REQUIREMENT SKETCH\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d20752c e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d20752c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-97c617a elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"97c617a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">2. IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3ea0f4f e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"3ea0f4f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-27a8db1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"27a8db1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The International Residential Code (IRC) sets safety and design standards for stairways in residential buildings, ensuring they meet structural, accessibility, and usability requirements. These guidelines help prevent accidents and improve comfort in homes.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IRC Stairway Regulations:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Maximum Riser Height<\\/strong>: Defines the height of each step to maintain consistency and ease of movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Minimum Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Ensures sufficient foot space for stability while ascending or descending.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1d689e0 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"1d689e0\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3428 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"1024\\\" height=\\\"590\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f5666db e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"f5666db\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3780e4a elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"3780e4a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Handrail Requirements<\\/strong>: Specifies height and graspability for added safety and support.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Guardrail Standards<\\/strong>: Prevents falls by establishing minimum railing height and spacing.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing Dimensions<\\/strong>: Regulates the size and placement of stair landings for safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Headroom Clearance<\\/strong>: Ensures adequate overhead space to prevent obstructions.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>These IRC rules play a crucial role in designing residential stairways that are both functional and compliant with safety standards.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ce18657 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ce18657\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-adc4321 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"adc4321\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">3. OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-55edcc6 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"55edcc6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-56630d5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"56630d5\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) is a U.S. government agency responsible for ensuring safe and healthy working conditions. Established in 1970 under the Occupational Safety and Health Act, OSHA sets regulations and conducts inspections to protect workers across various industries.<\\/p>\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) standard 1910.25 outlines safety requirements for stairways in workplaces to prevent accidents and ensure structural integrity. These regulations apply to various stair types, including standard, spiral, ship, and alternating tread stairs.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-10bffc2 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"10bffc2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3432 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ada56dd e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ada56dd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fd0407a e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"fd0407a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0f39eee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"0f39eee\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default elementor-inline-editing pen\\\" contenteditable=\\\"true\\\" spellcheck=\\\"false\\\" data-elementor-setting-key=\\\"title\\\" data-pen-placeholder=\\\"Type Here...\\\" data-qb-tmp-id=\\\"lt-738382\\\" data-gramm=\\\"false\\\">4. ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/h5>\\n<p>The Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) establishes accessibility standards for stairways to ensure safe and inclusive navigation for individuals with disabilities. These regulations apply to both interior and exterior stairs in public buildings and facilities.<br \\/>Key ADA Stairway Requirements:<br \\/><strong>Uniform Step Dimensions<\\/strong>: All steps must have consistent depth and height to prevent tripping hazards.<br \\/><strong>Step Height<\\/strong>: Must be between 5 and 7 inches for accessibility.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Minimum of 11 inches, measured from riser to riser, to provide secure footing.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Stair Width<\\/strong>: Must be at least 36 inches to accommodate users safely.<br \\/><strong>Handrails<\\/strong>: Required on both sides of stairways, positioned 34 to 38 inches above the stair nosing.<br \\/><strong>Nosings<\\/strong>: Must not project more than 1.5 inches beyond the riser below to reduce tripping risks.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-8baa50f elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"8baa50f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\u00a0<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-bbd2929 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"bbd2929\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c40a9f7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"c40a9f7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3469 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0c64e0e elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"0c64e0e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3465 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-57c9bd3 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"57c9bd3\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3477 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-e411696 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"e411696\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2fada2e elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"2fada2e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">5. PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2e1c457 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"2e1c457\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>PIP Civil, Structural, and Architectural (CSA) Practices publishes essential CSA Engineering Design Practices, including specifications and fabrication\\/installation details.<\\/p>\\n<p>This Practice provides fabrication and installation details for standard pipe railing for walking and working surfaces and for stair railing or handrail for egress. Although the details in this practice are intended to meet U.S. Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) requirements for process facilities, they may not meet the requirements of local or national building codes.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-82239ba e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"82239ba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-125261c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"125261c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section4\\\">4. CONCLUSION<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>Building codes for stairs are established to enhance safety for all users, including children, the elderly, and individuals with disabilities.<\\/p>\\n<p>They help minimize the risks of slips, trips, and falls while ensuring uniformity in design and construction for both contractors and homeowners.<\\/p>\\n<p>The codes outlined above play a crucial role in stair design and construction, with periodic updates to accommodate evolving safety standards and requirements.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1291,103,'_edit_last','1'),(1292,103,'_edit_lock','1746643455:1'),(1293,103,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1294,103,'_elementor_template_type','wp-post'),(1295,103,'_elementor_version','3.28.4'),(1296,803,'_wp_page_template','default'),(1297,803,'_thumbnail_id','1053'),(1298,803,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1299,803,'_elementor_template_type','wp-post'),(1300,803,'_elementor_version','3.28.4'),(1301,804,'_wp_page_template','default'),(1302,804,'_thumbnail_id','1053'),(1303,804,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1304,804,'_elementor_template_type','wp-post'),(1305,804,'_elementor_version','3.28.4'),(1306,103,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"130c3f42\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":[],\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"54818d70\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"editor\":\"<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ce11678 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ce11678\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-68c09ee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"68c09ee\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<div><em>Steel is essential for modern infrastructure because, it provides the basic structural framework behind every project \\u2013 industrial buildings, skyscrapers, bridges etc. Steel offers significant benefits in terms of greater durability, ease of installation, low carbon imprint and most importantly it can be reused-infinite times!!<\\/em><\\/div>\\n<div>Connection design plays a major role in ensuring secure, efficient connectors between structural steel components. A good connection design plays a vital role in ensuring building stability and overall safety. In this article, we have touched upon some key topics elaborating the significance of steel connection design in modern constructions.<br \\/><br \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-abad863 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"abad863\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-9b08814 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"9b08814\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2>Table of Contents<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ab6e4d6 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-mobile__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"ab6e4d6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section1\\\">Introduction<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section2\\\">Modelling Of Connections <\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section3\\\">Importance of connection design<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section4\\\">Advancement in connection design<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section5\\\">Conclusion<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-e4cf30e e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"e4cf30e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b7d6702 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"b7d6702\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fbc2e35 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"fbc2e35\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section1\\\">1. INTRODUCTION<\\/h2>\\n<div>Steel connection design is the process of creating connections between steel members to ensure the safety, stability and integrity of the structure. Connection designs are critical because they transfer forces between members and contribute significantly to the overall behaviour of the structure.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d18e894 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"d18e894\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3311 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-300x200.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-768x512.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1536x1024.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-2048x1366.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"1024\\\" height=\\\"683\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-300x200.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-768x512.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1536x1024.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-2048x1366.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3c6ee39 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"3c6ee39\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-58ffb32 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"58ffb32\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">\\u00a0<\\/h2>\\n<h2 id=\\\"section2\\\">2. MODELLING OF CONNECTIONS<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-14b6477 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"14b6477\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<div>Most structural engineering design jobs rely on both theoretical models and empirical evidence. The theory is translated into a design technique, which is then executed and tested. The findings from these trials are used to create new and more accurate analytical techniques, resulting in a greater understanding of how structures work. This is especially true for structural relationships. There is a high degree of uncertainty in the behavior of connections, which makes their analysis together, further increase the uncertainties in the connection. The consequence of this is that careful and accurate design of connections can be crucial to the design of the structure. The general design procedure can be summarized in four essential steps:<\\/div>\\n<ol>\\n<li>Calculation begins with determining the distribution of forces within the elements that will be connected. For beams carrying shear and moment, it is almost always assumed that the beam web carries the shear force while the beam flanges carry the bending moment. Once these are known, the flexibility of the connection\\u2019s components is evaluated. The flexibility is critical for determining the flow of forces via the connection.<\\/li>\\n<li>Design the components of the connection such that each force path has the required strength to transmit the forces.<\\/li>\\n<li>Ensure adequate ductility in the connection. This amounts to taking compatibility into account, because the above steps account only for force equilibrium.<\\/li>\\n<li>Check that serviceability requirements are met. Also check other factors such as fatigue resistance, fracture for welds, and corrosion protection<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-8d5ebe2 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"8d5ebe2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f451976 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"f451976\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">\\u00a0<\\/h2>\\n<h2 id=\\\"section3\\\">3. IMPORTANCE OF CONNECTION DESIGN<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-959083d elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"959083d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong><u>Structural integrity:<\\/u><\\/strong> Maintaining structural integrity throughout a structure\\u2019s life requires more than simply competent design. It serves as the \\u201cjoints\\u201d that allow forces to be transferred between structural components such as walls, floors, beams, and columns. We make sure buildings are dependable and serve the purpose for which they were intended throughout their lives.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong><u>Safety:<\\/u><\\/strong> Structural safety depends heavily on the connections, as they are often the most vulnerable points in the framework. Particularly during catastrophic events like earthquakes or strong winds, if connections are weak, it may cause a structure to collapse partially or completely. Safety measures in connection design ensure that structural systems remain robust, durable and resilient under various loads and environment conditions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong><u>Efficiency and cost:<\\/u><\\/strong> Efficient connection designs reduce material wastage and simplify the assembly process, saving both time and money. Choices for connections can reduce fabrication and installation time, improving the project\\u2019s overall efficiency. Calculate the required material quantities to avoid over-specification. Using high-strength materials can sometimes reduce the overall amount of material needed. Simplify connection designs to reduce fabrication and installation time. Employ advanced design and analysis software to optimize connection designs. These tools can help identify the most cost-effective solutions and reduce the time spent on manual calculations.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong><u>Durability and Maintenance:<\\/u><\\/strong> Well-designed connections resist corrosion, fatigue, and other types of wear over time, extending the life span of the structure and reducing maintenance needs.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong><u>Aesthetic and Architectural Flexibility:<\\/u><\\/strong> Modern architectural designs often demand exposed steel frameworks or specific visual aesthetics. Clever connection designs allow architects to realize complex and visually appealing structures without compromising strength or safety.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-09106e1 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"09106e1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a7dd6b7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"a7dd6b7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">\\u00a0<\\/h2>\\n<h2 id=\\\"section4\\\">4. ADVANCEMENT IN CONNECTION DESIGN<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a0b0961 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"a0b0961\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>Think, design, and build with structural steel\\u2014outside the box. There are several developed structural steel systems and products that go beyond conventional steel framing and that have, in many cases, changed the way designers approach projects. Some of them are shown below:<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-9444849 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"9444849\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-6ec7dd1 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"6ec7dd1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-aad6dc6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"aad6dc6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>a. <u>Hollo-Bolt:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<div>The Hollo-Bolt is the original expansion bolt for structural steel that is quickly and conveniently installed by simply inserting the fastener into a pre-drilled hole and tightening with a torque wrench, which reduces construction time and labour costs. The Hollo-Bolt is a faster alternative to welding or through-bolting hollow structural sections (HSS) or other steel members where access is restricted to one side.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d38eb45 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"d38eb45\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-5bb6dfe elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"5bb6dfe\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-3318 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2154px) 100vw, 2154px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png 2154w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-296x300.png 296w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1012x1024.png 1012w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-768x777.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1518x1536.png 1518w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-2024x2048.png 2024w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"2154\\\" height=\\\"2180\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png 2154w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-296x300.png 296w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1012x1024.png 1012w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-768x777.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1518x1536.png 1518w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-2024x2048.png 2024w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2154px) 100vw, 2154px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-6f43597 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"6f43597\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-cd4c41d e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"cd4c41d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ae8ed61 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"ae8ed61\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>b. <u>Girder Clamp:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<div>Girder Clamp is the world\\u2019s first and only structural steel clamping system approved by the International Code Council (ICC) and compliant with the International Building Code. A faster, cost-effective alternative to welding or drilling in the field, it is designed to reduce installation time and labour costs. A high-strength, permanent connection is quickly achieved by clamping two steel sections together.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b5b291a e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"b5b291a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c6b1b elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"c3c6b1b\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-3336 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-768x768.png 768w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"800\\\" height=\\\"800\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-768x768.png 768w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-67ee696 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"67ee696\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-41e0ec6 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"41e0ec6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-6ec3809 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"6ec3809\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>c. <u>Con-X:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<div>Con-X enables rapid design, fabrication, and assembly of robust, cost-efficient, and sustainable structures for the industrial, high-density residential, healthcare, data centre, and commercial markets. Con-X steel connections simply \\u201clower and lock\\u201d together in the field, allowing two-to four-times-faster assembly vs. conventional steel or concrete structures.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3ef73a2 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"3ef73a2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b0354bc elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"b0354bc\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3346 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-768x768.png 768w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"800\\\" height=\\\"800\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-768x768.png 768w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-59eed8c e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"59eed8c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a709af9 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"a709af9\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-860d20f elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"860d20f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>d. <u>Side Plate System:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<p>\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0 Side Plate Systems is the most experienced structural steel expert in the industry. This type\\u00a0 of procedure enhances a steel lateral design by utilizing unique connection designs that do not require any purchased components. Optimisation yields reduced steel tonnage, shorter erection times, and a cost-effective performance-based design. For the general contractor, Side Plate Systems becomes their extension in the design team. For the engineer, Side Plate Systems becomes the go-to source for steel structure optimization. Working closely with the fabricator, Side Plate Systems supplies detailing tools and hands-on assistance, ensuring the new, lighter, easier to erect steel package is the best job to run through the shop. In the field, erectors like our bolted connection designs that allow faster erection, mitigate weather delays that welded connections struggle with, and, of course, add strength to the building, resulting in high levels of resilience. Side Plate Systems brings a huge bonus to owners by delivering a lighter steel package, faster erection, and multiple areas of savings.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fe715bb e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"fe715bb\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f389131 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"f389131\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-3307 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2500px) 100vw, 2500px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png 2500w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-300x275.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1024x937.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-768x703.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1536x1406.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-2048x1874.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"2500\\\" height=\\\"2288\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png 2500w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-300x275.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1024x937.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-768x703.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1536x1406.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-2048x1874.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2500px) 100vw, 2500px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d4d6fff e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d4d6fff\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-80e9291 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"80e9291\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section5\\\">5. CONCLUSION<\\/h2>\\n<div>In steel structures, quality connection design is crucial because connections are the points where individual members intersect and transfer loads. \\u00a0A well-thought-out connection improves the structure\\u2019s durability, safety, and integrity. <strong>By minimizing possible weak points, a high-quality connection design ensures effective force distribution and lowers the chance of failure under stresses like wind, seismic activity, and normal operation<\\/strong>. \\u00a0Additionally, good design simplifies the construction process, decreases maintenance needs, and ultimately saves costs. In summary, strong connections are essential to a successful and dependable steel construction because they guarantee that the structure will function as planned for its life.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1307,805,'_wp_page_template','default'),(1308,805,'_thumbnail_id','1053'),(1309,805,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1310,805,'_elementor_template_type','wp-post'),(1311,805,'_elementor_version','3.28.4'),(1312,805,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"130c3f42\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":[],\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"54818d70\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"editor\":\"<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ce11678 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ce11678\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-68c09ee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"68c09ee\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<div><em>Steel is essential for modern infrastructure because, it provides the basic structural framework behind every project \\u2013 industrial buildings, skyscrapers, bridges etc. Steel offers significant benefits in terms of greater durability, ease of installation, low carbon imprint and most importantly it can be reused-infinite times!!<\\/em><\\/div>\\n<div>Connection design plays a major role in ensuring secure, efficient connectors between structural steel components. A good connection design plays a vital role in ensuring building stability and overall safety. In this article, we have touched upon some key topics elaborating the significance of steel connection design in modern constructions.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-abad863 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"abad863\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-9b08814 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"9b08814\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2>Table of Contents<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ab6e4d6 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-mobile__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"ab6e4d6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section1\\\">Introduction<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section2\\\">Modelling Of Connections <\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section3\\\">Importance of connection design<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section4\\\">Advancement in connection design<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section5\\\">Conclusion<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-e4cf30e e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"e4cf30e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b7d6702 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"b7d6702\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fbc2e35 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"fbc2e35\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section1\\\">1. INTRODUCTION<\\/h2>\\n<div>Steel connection design is the process of creating connections between steel members to ensure the safety, stability and integrity of the structure. Connection designs are critical because they transfer forces between members and contribute significantly to the overall behaviour of the structure.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d18e894 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"d18e894\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3311 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-300x200.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-768x512.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1536x1024.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-2048x1366.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"1024\\\" height=\\\"683\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-300x200.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-768x512.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1536x1024.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-2048x1366.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3c6ee39 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"3c6ee39\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-58ffb32 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"58ffb32\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">\\u00a0<\\/h2>\\n<h2 id=\\\"section2\\\">2. MODELLING OF CONNECTIONS<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-14b6477 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"14b6477\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<div>Most structural engineering design jobs rely on both theoretical models and empirical evidence. The theory is translated into a design technique, which is then executed and tested. The findings from these trials are used to create new and more accurate analytical techniques, resulting in a greater understanding of how structures work. This is especially true for structural relationships. There is a high degree of uncertainty in the behavior of connections, which makes their analysis together, further increase the uncertainties in the connection. The consequence of this is that careful and accurate design of connections can be crucial to the design of the structure. The general design procedure can be summarized in four essential steps:<\\/div>\\n<ol>\\n<li>Calculation begins with determining the distribution of forces within the elements that will be connected. For beams carrying shear and moment, it is almost always assumed that the beam web carries the shear force while the beam flanges carry the bending moment. Once these are known, the flexibility of the connection\\u2019s components is evaluated. The flexibility is critical for determining the flow of forces via the connection.<\\/li>\\n<li>Design the components of the connection such that each force path has the required strength to transmit the forces.<\\/li>\\n<li>Ensure adequate ductility in the connection. This amounts to taking compatibility into account, because the above steps account only for force equilibrium.<\\/li>\\n<li>Check that serviceability requirements are met. Also check other factors such as fatigue resistance, fracture for welds, and corrosion protection<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-8d5ebe2 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"8d5ebe2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f451976 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"f451976\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">\\u00a0<\\/h2>\\n<h2 id=\\\"section3\\\">3. IMPORTANCE OF CONNECTION DESIGN<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-959083d elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"959083d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong><u>Structural integrity:<\\/u><\\/strong> Maintaining structural integrity throughout a structure\\u2019s life requires more than simply competent design. It serves as the \\u201cjoints\\u201d that allow forces to be transferred between structural components such as walls, floors, beams, and columns. We make sure buildings are dependable and serve the purpose for which they were intended throughout their lives.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong><u>Safety:<\\/u><\\/strong> Structural safety depends heavily on the connections, as they are often the most vulnerable points in the framework. Particularly during catastrophic events like earthquakes or strong winds, if connections are weak, it may cause a structure to collapse partially or completely. Safety measures in connection design ensure that structural systems remain robust, durable and resilient under various loads and environment conditions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong><u>Efficiency and cost:<\\/u><\\/strong> Efficient connection designs reduce material wastage and simplify the assembly process, saving both time and money. Choices for connections can reduce fabrication and installation time, improving the project\\u2019s overall efficiency. Calculate the required material quantities to avoid over-specification. Using high-strength materials can sometimes reduce the overall amount of material needed. Simplify connection designs to reduce fabrication and installation time. Employ advanced design and analysis software to optimize connection designs. These tools can help identify the most cost-effective solutions and reduce the time spent on manual calculations.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong><u>Durability and Maintenance:<\\/u><\\/strong> Well-designed connections resist corrosion, fatigue, and other types of wear over time, extending the life span of the structure and reducing maintenance needs.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong><u>Aesthetic and Architectural Flexibility:<\\/u><\\/strong> Modern architectural designs often demand exposed steel frameworks or specific visual aesthetics. Clever connection designs allow architects to realize complex and visually appealing structures without compromising strength or safety.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-09106e1 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"09106e1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a7dd6b7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"a7dd6b7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">\\u00a0<\\/h2>\\n<h2 id=\\\"section4\\\">4. ADVANCEMENT IN CONNECTION DESIGN<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a0b0961 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"a0b0961\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>Think, design, and build with structural steel\\u2014outside the box. There are several developed structural steel systems and products that go beyond conventional steel framing and that have, in many cases, changed the way designers approach projects. Some of them are shown below:<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-9444849 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"9444849\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-6ec7dd1 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"6ec7dd1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-aad6dc6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"aad6dc6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>a. <u>Hollo-Bolt:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<div>The Hollo-Bolt is the original expansion bolt for structural steel that is quickly and conveniently installed by simply inserting the fastener into a pre-drilled hole and tightening with a torque wrench, which reduces construction time and labour costs. The Hollo-Bolt is a faster alternative to welding or through-bolting hollow structural sections (HSS) or other steel members where access is restricted to one side.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d38eb45 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"d38eb45\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-5bb6dfe elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"5bb6dfe\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-3318 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2154px) 100vw, 2154px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png 2154w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-296x300.png 296w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1012x1024.png 1012w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-768x777.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1518x1536.png 1518w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-2024x2048.png 2024w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"2154\\\" height=\\\"2180\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png 2154w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-296x300.png 296w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1012x1024.png 1012w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-768x777.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1518x1536.png 1518w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-2024x2048.png 2024w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2154px) 100vw, 2154px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-6f43597 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"6f43597\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-cd4c41d e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"cd4c41d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ae8ed61 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"ae8ed61\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>b. <u>Girder Clamp:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<div>Girder Clamp is the world\\u2019s first and only structural steel clamping system approved by the International Code Council (ICC) and compliant with the International Building Code. A faster, cost-effective alternative to welding or drilling in the field, it is designed to reduce installation time and labour costs. A high-strength, permanent connection is quickly achieved by clamping two steel sections together.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b5b291a e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"b5b291a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c6b1b elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"c3c6b1b\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-3336 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-768x768.png 768w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"800\\\" height=\\\"800\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-768x768.png 768w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-67ee696 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"67ee696\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-41e0ec6 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"41e0ec6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-6ec3809 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"6ec3809\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>c. <u>Con-X:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<div>Con-X enables rapid design, fabrication, and assembly of robust, cost-efficient, and sustainable structures for the industrial, high-density residential, healthcare, data centre, and commercial markets. Con-X steel connections simply \\u201clower and lock\\u201d together in the field, allowing two-to four-times-faster assembly vs. conventional steel or concrete structures.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3ef73a2 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"3ef73a2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b0354bc elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"b0354bc\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3346 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-768x768.png 768w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"800\\\" height=\\\"800\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-768x768.png 768w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-59eed8c e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"59eed8c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a709af9 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"a709af9\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-860d20f elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"860d20f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>d. <u>Side Plate System:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<p>\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0 Side Plate Systems is the most experienced structural steel expert in the industry. This type\\u00a0 of procedure enhances a steel lateral design by utilizing unique connection designs that do not require any purchased components. Optimisation yields reduced steel tonnage, shorter erection times, and a cost-effective performance-based design. For the general contractor, Side Plate Systems becomes their extension in the design team. For the engineer, Side Plate Systems becomes the go-to source for steel structure optimization. Working closely with the fabricator, Side Plate Systems supplies detailing tools and hands-on assistance, ensuring the new, lighter, easier to erect steel package is the best job to run through the shop. In the field, erectors like our bolted connection designs that allow faster erection, mitigate weather delays that welded connections struggle with, and, of course, add strength to the building, resulting in high levels of resilience. Side Plate Systems brings a huge bonus to owners by delivering a lighter steel package, faster erection, and multiple areas of savings.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fe715bb e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"fe715bb\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f389131 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"f389131\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-3307 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2500px) 100vw, 2500px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png 2500w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-300x275.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1024x937.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-768x703.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1536x1406.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-2048x1874.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"2500\\\" height=\\\"2288\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png 2500w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-300x275.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1024x937.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-768x703.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1536x1406.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-2048x1874.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2500px) 100vw, 2500px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d4d6fff e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d4d6fff\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-80e9291 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"80e9291\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section5\\\">5. CONCLUSION<\\/h2>\\n<div>In steel structures, quality connection design is crucial because connections are the points where individual members intersect and transfer loads. \\u00a0A well-thought-out connection improves the structure\\u2019s durability, safety, and integrity. <strong>By minimizing possible weak points, a high-quality connection design ensures effective force distribution and lowers the chance of failure under stresses like wind, seismic activity, and normal operation<\\/strong>. \\u00a0Additionally, good design simplifies the construction process, decreases maintenance needs, and ultimately saves costs. In summary, strong connections are essential to a successful and dependable steel construction because they guarantee that the structure will function as planned for its life.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1314,806,'_wp_page_template','default'),(1315,806,'_thumbnail_id','1053'),(1316,806,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1317,806,'_elementor_template_type','wp-post'),(1318,806,'_elementor_version','3.28.4'),(1319,806,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"130c3f42\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":[],\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"54818d70\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"editor\":\"<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ce11678 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ce11678\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-68c09ee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"68c09ee\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<div><em>Steel is essential for modern infrastructure because, it provides the basic structural framework behind every project \\u2013 industrial buildings, skyscrapers, bridges etc. Steel offers significant benefits in terms of greater durability, ease of installation, low carbon imprint and most importantly it can be reused-infinite times!!<\\/em><\\/div>\\n<div>Connection design plays a major role in ensuring secure, efficient connectors between structural steel components. A good connection design plays a vital role in ensuring building stability and overall safety. In this article, we have touched upon some key topics elaborating the significance of steel connection design in modern constructions.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-abad863 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"abad863\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-9b08814 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"9b08814\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2>Table of Contents<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ab6e4d6 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-mobile__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"ab6e4d6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section1\\\">Introduction<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section2\\\">Modelling Of Connections <\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section3\\\">Importance of connection design<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section4\\\">Advancement in connection design<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section5\\\">Conclusion<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-e4cf30e e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"e4cf30e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b7d6702 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"b7d6702\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fbc2e35 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"fbc2e35\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section1\\\">1. INTRODUCTION<\\/h2>\\n<div>Steel connection design is the process of creating connections between steel members to ensure the safety, stability and integrity of the structure. Connection designs are critical because they transfer forces between members and contribute significantly to the overall behaviour of the structure.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d18e894 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"d18e894\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3311 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-300x200.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-768x512.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1536x1024.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-2048x1366.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"1024\\\" height=\\\"683\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-300x200.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-768x512.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1536x1024.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-2048x1366.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3c6ee39 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"3c6ee39\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-58ffb32 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"58ffb32\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">\\u00a0<\\/h2>\\n<h2 id=\\\"section2\\\">2. MODELLING OF CONNECTIONS<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-14b6477 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"14b6477\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<div>Most structural engineering design jobs rely on both theoretical models and empirical evidence. The theory is translated into a design technique, which is then executed and tested. The findings from these trials are used to create new and more accurate analytical techniques, resulting in a greater understanding of how structures work. This is especially true for structural relationships. There is a high degree of uncertainty in the behavior of connections, which makes their analysis together, further increase the uncertainties in the connection. The consequence of this is that careful and accurate design of connections can be crucial to the design of the structure. The general design procedure can be summarized in four essential steps:<\\/div>\\n<ol>\\n<li>Calculation begins with determining the distribution of forces within the elements that will be connected. For beams carrying shear and moment, it is almost always assumed that the beam web carries the shear force while the beam flanges carry the bending moment. Once these are known, the flexibility of the connection\\u2019s components is evaluated. The flexibility is critical for determining the flow of forces via the connection.<\\/li>\\n<li>Design the components of the connection such that each force path has the required strength to transmit the forces.<\\/li>\\n<li>Ensure adequate ductility in the connection. This amounts to taking compatibility into account, because the above steps account only for force equilibrium.<\\/li>\\n<li>Check that serviceability requirements are met. Also check other factors such as fatigue resistance, fracture for welds, and corrosion protection<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-8d5ebe2 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"8d5ebe2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f451976 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"f451976\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">\\u00a0<\\/h2>\\n<h2 id=\\\"section3\\\">3. IMPORTANCE OF CONNECTION DESIGN<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-959083d elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"959083d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong><u>Structural integrity:<\\/u><\\/strong> Maintaining structural integrity throughout a structure\\u2019s life requires more than simply competent design. It serves as the \\u201cjoints\\u201d that allow forces to be transferred between structural components such as walls, floors, beams, and columns. We make sure buildings are dependable and serve the purpose for which they were intended throughout their lives.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong><u>Safety:<\\/u><\\/strong> Structural safety depends heavily on the connections, as they are often the most vulnerable points in the framework. Particularly during catastrophic events like earthquakes or strong winds, if connections are weak, it may cause a structure to collapse partially or completely. Safety measures in connection design ensure that structural systems remain robust, durable and resilient under various loads and environment conditions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong><u>Efficiency and cost:<\\/u><\\/strong> Efficient connection designs reduce material wastage and simplify the assembly process, saving both time and money. Choices for connections can reduce fabrication and installation time, improving the project\\u2019s overall efficiency. Calculate the required material quantities to avoid over-specification. Using high-strength materials can sometimes reduce the overall amount of material needed. Simplify connection designs to reduce fabrication and installation time. Employ advanced design and analysis software to optimize connection designs. These tools can help identify the most cost-effective solutions and reduce the time spent on manual calculations.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong><u>Durability and Maintenance:<\\/u><\\/strong> Well-designed connections resist corrosion, fatigue, and other types of wear over time, extending the life span of the structure and reducing maintenance needs.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong><u>Aesthetic and Architectural Flexibility:<\\/u><\\/strong> Modern architectural designs often demand exposed steel frameworks or specific visual aesthetics. Clever connection designs allow architects to realize complex and visually appealing structures without compromising strength or safety.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-09106e1 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"09106e1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a7dd6b7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"a7dd6b7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">\\u00a0<\\/h2>\\n<h2 id=\\\"section4\\\">4. ADVANCEMENT IN CONNECTION DESIGN<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a0b0961 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"a0b0961\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>Think, design, and build with structural steel\\u2014outside the box. There are several developed structural steel systems and products that go beyond conventional steel framing and that have, in many cases, changed the way designers approach projects. Some of them are shown below:<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-9444849 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"9444849\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-6ec7dd1 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"6ec7dd1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-aad6dc6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"aad6dc6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>a. <u>Hollo-Bolt:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<div>The Hollo-Bolt is the original expansion bolt for structural steel that is quickly and conveniently installed by simply inserting the fastener into a pre-drilled hole and tightening with a torque wrench, which reduces construction time and labour costs. The Hollo-Bolt is a faster alternative to welding or through-bolting hollow structural sections (HSS) or other steel members where access is restricted to one side.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d38eb45 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"d38eb45\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-5bb6dfe elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"5bb6dfe\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-3318 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2154px) 100vw, 2154px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png 2154w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-296x300.png 296w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1012x1024.png 1012w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-768x777.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1518x1536.png 1518w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-2024x2048.png 2024w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"2154\\\" height=\\\"2180\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png 2154w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-296x300.png 296w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1012x1024.png 1012w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-768x777.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1518x1536.png 1518w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-2024x2048.png 2024w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2154px) 100vw, 2154px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-6f43597 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"6f43597\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-cd4c41d e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"cd4c41d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ae8ed61 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"ae8ed61\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>b. <u>Girder Clamp:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<div>Girder Clamp is the world\\u2019s first and only structural steel clamping system approved by the International Code Council (ICC) and compliant with the International Building Code. A faster, cost-effective alternative to welding or drilling in the field, it is designed to reduce installation time and labour costs. A high-strength, permanent connection is quickly achieved by clamping two steel sections together.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b5b291a e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"b5b291a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c6b1b elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"c3c6b1b\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-3336 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-768x768.png 768w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"800\\\" height=\\\"800\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-768x768.png 768w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-67ee696 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"67ee696\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-41e0ec6 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"41e0ec6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-6ec3809 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"6ec3809\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>c. <u>Con-X:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<div>Con-X enables rapid design, fabrication, and assembly of robust, cost-efficient, and sustainable structures for the industrial, high-density residential, healthcare, data centre, and commercial markets. Con-X steel connections simply \\u201clower and lock\\u201d together in the field, allowing two-to four-times-faster assembly vs. conventional steel or concrete structures.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3ef73a2 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"3ef73a2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b0354bc elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"b0354bc\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3346 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-768x768.png 768w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"800\\\" height=\\\"800\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-768x768.png 768w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-59eed8c e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"59eed8c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a709af9 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"a709af9\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-860d20f elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"860d20f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>d. <u>Side Plate System:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<p>\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0 Side Plate Systems is the most experienced structural steel expert in the industry. This type\\u00a0 of procedure enhances a steel lateral design by utilizing unique connection designs that do not require any purchased components. Optimisation yields reduced steel tonnage, shorter erection times, and a cost-effective performance-based design. For the general contractor, Side Plate Systems becomes their extension in the design team. For the engineer, Side Plate Systems becomes the go-to source for steel structure optimization. Working closely with the fabricator, Side Plate Systems supplies detailing tools and hands-on assistance, ensuring the new, lighter, easier to erect steel package is the best job to run through the shop. In the field, erectors like our bolted connection designs that allow faster erection, mitigate weather delays that welded connections struggle with, and, of course, add strength to the building, resulting in high levels of resilience. Side Plate Systems brings a huge bonus to owners by delivering a lighter steel package, faster erection, and multiple areas of savings.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fe715bb e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"fe715bb\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f389131 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"f389131\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-3307 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2500px) 100vw, 2500px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png 2500w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-300x275.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1024x937.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-768x703.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1536x1406.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-2048x1874.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"2500\\\" height=\\\"2288\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png 2500w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-300x275.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1024x937.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-768x703.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1536x1406.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-2048x1874.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2500px) 100vw, 2500px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d4d6fff e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d4d6fff\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-80e9291 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"80e9291\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section5\\\">5. CONCLUSION<\\/h2>\\n<div>In steel structures, quality connection design is crucial because connections are the points where individual members intersect and transfer loads. \\u00a0A well-thought-out connection improves the structure\\u2019s durability, safety, and integrity. <strong>By minimizing possible weak points, a high-quality connection design ensures effective force distribution and lowers the chance of failure under stresses like wind, seismic activity, and normal operation<\\/strong>. \\u00a0Additionally, good design simplifies the construction process, decreases maintenance needs, and ultimately saves costs. In summary, strong connections are essential to a successful and dependable steel construction because they guarantee that the structure will function as planned for its life.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1321,807,'_wp_page_template','default'),(1322,807,'_thumbnail_id','1053'),(1323,807,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1324,807,'_elementor_template_type','wp-post'),(1325,807,'_elementor_version','3.28.4'),(1326,807,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"130c3f42\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":[],\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"54818d70\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"editor\":\"<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ce11678 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ce11678\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-68c09ee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"68c09ee\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<div><em>Steel is essential for modern infrastructure because, it provides the basic structural framework behind every project \\u2013 industrial buildings, skyscrapers, bridges etc. Steel offers significant benefits in terms of greater durability, ease of installation, low carbon imprint and most importantly it can be reused-infinite times!!<\\/em><\\/div>\\n<div>Connection design plays a major role in ensuring secure, efficient connectors between structural steel components. A good connection design plays a vital role in ensuring building stability and overall safety. In this article, we have touched upon some key topics elaborating the significance of steel connection design in modern constructions.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-abad863 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"abad863\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-9b08814 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"9b08814\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2>Table of Contents<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ab6e4d6 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-mobile__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"ab6e4d6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section1\\\">Introduction<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section2\\\">Modelling Of Connections <\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section3\\\">Importance of connection design<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section4\\\">Advancement in connection design<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section5\\\">Conclusion<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-e4cf30e e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"e4cf30e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b7d6702 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"b7d6702\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fbc2e35 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"fbc2e35\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section1\\\">1. INTRODUCTION<\\/h2>\\n<div>Steel connection design is the process of creating connections between steel members to ensure the safety, stability and integrity of the structure. Connection designs are critical because they transfer forces between members and contribute significantly to the overall behaviour of the structure.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d18e894 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"d18e894\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3311 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-300x200.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-768x512.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1536x1024.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-2048x1366.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"1024\\\" height=\\\"683\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-300x200.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-768x512.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1536x1024.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-2048x1366.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3c6ee39 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"3c6ee39\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-58ffb32 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"58ffb32\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">\\u00a0<\\/h2>\\n<h2 id=\\\"section2\\\">2. MODELLING OF CONNECTIONS<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-14b6477 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"14b6477\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<div>Most structural engineering design jobs rely on both theoretical models and empirical evidence. The theory is translated into a design technique, which is then executed and tested. The findings from these trials are used to create new and more accurate analytical techniques, resulting in a greater understanding of how structures work. This is especially true for structural relationships. There is a high degree of uncertainty in the behavior of connections, which makes their analysis together, further increase the uncertainties in the connection. The consequence of this is that careful and accurate design of connections can be crucial to the design of the structure. The general design procedure can be summarized in four essential steps:<\\/div>\\n<ol>\\n<li>Calculation begins with determining the distribution of forces within the elements that will be connected. For beams carrying shear and moment, it is almost always assumed that the beam web carries the shear force while the beam flanges carry the bending moment. Once these are known, the flexibility of the connection\\u2019s components is evaluated. The flexibility is critical for determining the flow of forces via the connection.<\\/li>\\n<li>Design the components of the connection such that each force path has the required strength to transmit the forces.<\\/li>\\n<li>Ensure adequate ductility in the connection. This amounts to taking compatibility into account, because the above steps account only for force equilibrium.<\\/li>\\n<li>Check that serviceability requirements are met. Also check other factors such as fatigue resistance, fracture for welds, and corrosion protection<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-8d5ebe2 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"8d5ebe2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f451976 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"f451976\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">\\u00a0<\\/h2>\\n<h2 id=\\\"section3\\\">3. IMPORTANCE OF CONNECTION DESIGN<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-959083d elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"959083d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong><u>Structural integrity:<\\/u><\\/strong> Maintaining structural integrity throughout a structure\\u2019s life requires more than simply competent design. It serves as the \\u201cjoints\\u201d that allow forces to be transferred between structural components such as walls, floors, beams, and columns. We make sure buildings are dependable and serve the purpose for which they were intended throughout their lives.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong><u>Safety:<\\/u><\\/strong> Structural safety depends heavily on the connections, as they are often the most vulnerable points in the framework. Particularly during catastrophic events like earthquakes or strong winds, if connections are weak, it may cause a structure to collapse partially or completely. Safety measures in connection design ensure that structural systems remain robust, durable and resilient under various loads and environment conditions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong><u>Efficiency and cost:<\\/u><\\/strong> Efficient connection designs reduce material wastage and simplify the assembly process, saving both time and money. Choices for connections can reduce fabrication and installation time, improving the project\\u2019s overall efficiency. Calculate the required material quantities to avoid over-specification. Using high-strength materials can sometimes reduce the overall amount of material needed. Simplify connection designs to reduce fabrication and installation time. Employ advanced design and analysis software to optimize connection designs. These tools can help identify the most cost-effective solutions and reduce the time spent on manual calculations.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong><u>Durability and Maintenance:<\\/u><\\/strong> Well-designed connections resist corrosion, fatigue, and other types of wear over time, extending the life span of the structure and reducing maintenance needs.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong><u>Aesthetic and Architectural Flexibility:<\\/u><\\/strong> Modern architectural designs often demand exposed steel frameworks or specific visual aesthetics. Clever connection designs allow architects to realize complex and visually appealing structures without compromising strength or safety.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-09106e1 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"09106e1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a7dd6b7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"a7dd6b7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">\\u00a0<\\/h2>\\n<h2 id=\\\"section4\\\">4. ADVANCEMENT IN CONNECTION DESIGN<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a0b0961 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"a0b0961\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>Think, design, and build with structural steel\\u2014outside the box. There are several developed structural steel systems and products that go beyond conventional steel framing and that have, in many cases, changed the way designers approach projects. Some of them are shown below:<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-9444849 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"9444849\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-6ec7dd1 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"6ec7dd1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-aad6dc6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"aad6dc6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>a. <u>Hollo-Bolt:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<div>The Hollo-Bolt is the original expansion bolt for structural steel that is quickly and conveniently installed by simply inserting the fastener into a pre-drilled hole and tightening with a torque wrench, which reduces construction time and labour costs. The Hollo-Bolt is a faster alternative to welding or through-bolting hollow structural sections (HSS) or other steel members where access is restricted to one side.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d38eb45 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"d38eb45\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-5bb6dfe elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"5bb6dfe\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-3318 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2154px) 100vw, 2154px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png 2154w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-296x300.png 296w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1012x1024.png 1012w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-768x777.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1518x1536.png 1518w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-2024x2048.png 2024w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"2154\\\" height=\\\"2180\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png 2154w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-296x300.png 296w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1012x1024.png 1012w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-768x777.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1518x1536.png 1518w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-2024x2048.png 2024w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2154px) 100vw, 2154px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-6f43597 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"6f43597\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-cd4c41d e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"cd4c41d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ae8ed61 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"ae8ed61\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>b. <u>Girder Clamp:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<div>Girder Clamp is the world\\u2019s first and only structural steel clamping system approved by the International Code Council (ICC) and compliant with the International Building Code. A faster, cost-effective alternative to welding or drilling in the field, it is designed to reduce installation time and labour costs. A high-strength, permanent connection is quickly achieved by clamping two steel sections together.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b5b291a e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"b5b291a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c6b1b elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"c3c6b1b\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-3336 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-768x768.png 768w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"800\\\" height=\\\"800\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-768x768.png 768w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-67ee696 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"67ee696\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-41e0ec6 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"41e0ec6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-6ec3809 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"6ec3809\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>c. <u>Con-X:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<div>Con-X enables rapid design, fabrication, and assembly of robust, cost-efficient, and sustainable structures for the industrial, high-density residential, healthcare, data centre, and commercial markets. Con-X steel connections simply \\u201clower and lock\\u201d together in the field, allowing two-to four-times-faster assembly vs. conventional steel or concrete structures.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3ef73a2 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"3ef73a2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b0354bc elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"b0354bc\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3346 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-768x768.png 768w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"800\\\" height=\\\"800\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-768x768.png 768w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-59eed8c e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"59eed8c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a709af9 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"a709af9\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-860d20f elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"860d20f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>d. <u>Side Plate System:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<p>\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0 Side Plate Systems is the most experienced structural steel expert in the industry. This type\\u00a0 of procedure enhances a steel lateral design by utilizing unique connection designs that do not require any purchased components. Optimisation yields reduced steel tonnage, shorter erection times, and a cost-effective performance-based design. For the general contractor, Side Plate Systems becomes their extension in the design team. For the engineer, Side Plate Systems becomes the go-to source for steel structure optimization. Working closely with the fabricator, Side Plate Systems supplies detailing tools and hands-on assistance, ensuring the new, lighter, easier to erect steel package is the best job to run through the shop. In the field, erectors like our bolted connection designs that allow faster erection, mitigate weather delays that welded connections struggle with, and, of course, add strength to the building, resulting in high levels of resilience. Side Plate Systems brings a huge bonus to owners by delivering a lighter steel package, faster erection, and multiple areas of savings.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fe715bb e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"fe715bb\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f389131 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"f389131\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-3307 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2500px) 100vw, 2500px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png 2500w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-300x275.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1024x937.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-768x703.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1536x1406.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-2048x1874.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"2500\\\" height=\\\"2288\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png 2500w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-300x275.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1024x937.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-768x703.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1536x1406.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-2048x1874.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2500px) 100vw, 2500px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d4d6fff e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d4d6fff\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-80e9291 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"80e9291\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section5\\\">5. CONCLUSION<\\/h2>\\n<div>In steel structures, quality connection design is crucial because connections are the points where individual members intersect and transfer loads. \\u00a0A well-thought-out connection improves the structure\\u2019s durability, safety, and integrity. <strong>By minimizing possible weak points, a high-quality connection design ensures effective force distribution and lowers the chance of failure under stresses like wind, seismic activity, and normal operation<\\/strong>. \\u00a0Additionally, good design simplifies the construction process, decreases maintenance needs, and ultimately saves costs. In summary, strong connections are essential to a successful and dependable steel construction because they guarantee that the structure will function as planned for its life.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1328,808,'_wp_page_template','default'),(1329,808,'_thumbnail_id','1053'),(1330,808,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1331,808,'_elementor_template_type','wp-post'),(1332,808,'_elementor_version','3.28.4'),(1333,808,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"130c3f42\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":[],\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"54818d70\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"editor\":\"<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ce11678 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ce11678\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-68c09ee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"68c09ee\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<div><em>Steel is essential for modern infrastructure because, it provides the basic structural framework behind every project \\u2013 industrial buildings, skyscrapers, bridges etc. Steel offers significant benefits in terms of greater durability, ease of installation, low carbon imprint and most importantly it can be reused-infinite times!!<\\/em><\\/div>\\n<div>Connection design plays a major role in ensuring secure, efficient connectors between structural steel components. A good connection design plays a vital role in ensuring building stability and overall safety. In this article, we have touched upon some key topics elaborating the significance of steel connection design in modern constructions.<br \\/><br \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-abad863 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"abad863\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-9b08814 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"9b08814\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2>Table of Contents<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ab6e4d6 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-mobile__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"ab6e4d6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section1\\\">Introduction<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section2\\\">Modelling Of Connections <\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section3\\\">Importance of connection design<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section4\\\">Advancement in connection design<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/holistic-approach-of-steel-connection-design\\/#section5\\\">Conclusion<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-e4cf30e e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"e4cf30e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b7d6702 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"b7d6702\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fbc2e35 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"fbc2e35\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section1\\\">1. INTRODUCTION<\\/h2>\\n<div>Steel connection design is the process of creating connections between steel members to ensure the safety, stability and integrity of the structure. Connection designs are critical because they transfer forces between members and contribute significantly to the overall behaviour of the structure.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d18e894 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"d18e894\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3311 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-300x200.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-768x512.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1536x1024.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-2048x1366.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"1024\\\" height=\\\"683\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1024x683.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-300x200.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-768x512.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-1536x1024.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Connection-design-e1736335745556-2048x1366.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3c6ee39 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"3c6ee39\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-58ffb32 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"58ffb32\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">\\u00a0<\\/h2>\\n<h2 id=\\\"section2\\\">2. MODELLING OF CONNECTIONS<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-14b6477 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"14b6477\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<div>Most structural engineering design jobs rely on both theoretical models and empirical evidence. The theory is translated into a design technique, which is then executed and tested. The findings from these trials are used to create new and more accurate analytical techniques, resulting in a greater understanding of how structures work. This is especially true for structural relationships. There is a high degree of uncertainty in the behavior of connections, which makes their analysis together, further increase the uncertainties in the connection. The consequence of this is that careful and accurate design of connections can be crucial to the design of the structure. The general design procedure can be summarized in four essential steps:<\\/div>\\n<ol>\\n<li>Calculation begins with determining the distribution of forces within the elements that will be connected. For beams carrying shear and moment, it is almost always assumed that the beam web carries the shear force while the beam flanges carry the bending moment. Once these are known, the flexibility of the connection\\u2019s components is evaluated. The flexibility is critical for determining the flow of forces via the connection.<\\/li>\\n<li>Design the components of the connection such that each force path has the required strength to transmit the forces.<\\/li>\\n<li>Ensure adequate ductility in the connection. This amounts to taking compatibility into account, because the above steps account only for force equilibrium.<\\/li>\\n<li>Check that serviceability requirements are met. Also check other factors such as fatigue resistance, fracture for welds, and corrosion protection<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-8d5ebe2 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"8d5ebe2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f451976 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"f451976\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">\\u00a0<\\/h2>\\n<h2 id=\\\"section3\\\">3. IMPORTANCE OF CONNECTION DESIGN<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-959083d elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"959083d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong><u>Structural integrity:<\\/u><\\/strong> Maintaining structural integrity throughout a structure\\u2019s life requires more than simply competent design. It serves as the \\u201cjoints\\u201d that allow forces to be transferred between structural components such as walls, floors, beams, and columns. We make sure buildings are dependable and serve the purpose for which they were intended throughout their lives.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong><u>Safety:<\\/u><\\/strong> Structural safety depends heavily on the connections, as they are often the most vulnerable points in the framework. Particularly during catastrophic events like earthquakes or strong winds, if connections are weak, it may cause a structure to collapse partially or completely. Safety measures in connection design ensure that structural systems remain robust, durable and resilient under various loads and environment conditions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong><u>Efficiency and cost:<\\/u><\\/strong> Efficient connection designs reduce material wastage and simplify the assembly process, saving both time and money. Choices for connections can reduce fabrication and installation time, improving the project\\u2019s overall efficiency. Calculate the required material quantities to avoid over-specification. Using high-strength materials can sometimes reduce the overall amount of material needed. Simplify connection designs to reduce fabrication and installation time. Employ advanced design and analysis software to optimize connection designs. These tools can help identify the most cost-effective solutions and reduce the time spent on manual calculations.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong><u>Durability and Maintenance:<\\/u><\\/strong> Well-designed connections resist corrosion, fatigue, and other types of wear over time, extending the life span of the structure and reducing maintenance needs.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong><u>Aesthetic and Architectural Flexibility:<\\/u><\\/strong> Modern architectural designs often demand exposed steel frameworks or specific visual aesthetics. Clever connection designs allow architects to realize complex and visually appealing structures without compromising strength or safety.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-09106e1 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"09106e1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a7dd6b7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"a7dd6b7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">\\u00a0<\\/h2>\\n<h2 id=\\\"section4\\\">4. ADVANCEMENT IN CONNECTION DESIGN<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a0b0961 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"a0b0961\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>Think, design, and build with structural steel\\u2014outside the box. There are several developed structural steel systems and products that go beyond conventional steel framing and that have, in many cases, changed the way designers approach projects. Some of them are shown below:<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-9444849 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"9444849\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-6ec7dd1 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"6ec7dd1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-aad6dc6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"aad6dc6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>a. <u>Hollo-Bolt:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<div>The Hollo-Bolt is the original expansion bolt for structural steel that is quickly and conveniently installed by simply inserting the fastener into a pre-drilled hole and tightening with a torque wrench, which reduces construction time and labour costs. The Hollo-Bolt is a faster alternative to welding or through-bolting hollow structural sections (HSS) or other steel members where access is restricted to one side.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d38eb45 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"d38eb45\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-5bb6dfe elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"5bb6dfe\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-3318 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2154px) 100vw, 2154px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png 2154w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-296x300.png 296w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1012x1024.png 1012w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-768x777.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1518x1536.png 1518w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-2024x2048.png 2024w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"2154\\\" height=\\\"2180\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493.png 2154w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-296x300.png 296w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1012x1024.png 1012w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-768x777.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-1518x1536.png 1518w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Holo-bolt-e1736337200493-2024x2048.png 2024w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2154px) 100vw, 2154px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-6f43597 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"6f43597\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-cd4c41d e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"cd4c41d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ae8ed61 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"ae8ed61\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>b. <u>Girder Clamp:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<div>Girder Clamp is the world\\u2019s first and only structural steel clamping system approved by the International Code Council (ICC) and compliant with the International Building Code. A faster, cost-effective alternative to welding or drilling in the field, it is designed to reduce installation time and labour costs. A high-strength, permanent connection is quickly achieved by clamping two steel sections together.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b5b291a e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"b5b291a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c3c6b1b elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"c3c6b1b\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-3336 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-768x768.png 768w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"800\\\" height=\\\"800\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Girder-Clamp-2-768x768.png 768w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-67ee696 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"67ee696\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-41e0ec6 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"41e0ec6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-6ec3809 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"6ec3809\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>c. <u>Con-X:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<div>Con-X enables rapid design, fabrication, and assembly of robust, cost-efficient, and sustainable structures for the industrial, high-density residential, healthcare, data centre, and commercial markets. Con-X steel connections simply \\u201clower and lock\\u201d together in the field, allowing two-to four-times-faster assembly vs. conventional steel or concrete structures.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3ef73a2 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"3ef73a2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b0354bc elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"b0354bc\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3346 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-768x768.png 768w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"800\\\" height=\\\"800\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x.png 800w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-300x300.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-150x150.png 150w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/con-x-768x768.png 768w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-59eed8c e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"59eed8c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a709af9 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"a709af9\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-860d20f elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"860d20f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><strong>d. <u>Side Plate System:<\\/u><\\/strong>\\n<p>\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0\\u00a0 Side Plate Systems is the most experienced structural steel expert in the industry. This type\\u00a0 of procedure enhances a steel lateral design by utilizing unique connection designs that do not require any purchased components. Optimisation yields reduced steel tonnage, shorter erection times, and a cost-effective performance-based design. For the general contractor, Side Plate Systems becomes their extension in the design team. For the engineer, Side Plate Systems becomes the go-to source for steel structure optimization. Working closely with the fabricator, Side Plate Systems supplies detailing tools and hands-on assistance, ensuring the new, lighter, easier to erect steel package is the best job to run through the shop. In the field, erectors like our bolted connection designs that allow faster erection, mitigate weather delays that welded connections struggle with, and, of course, add strength to the building, resulting in high levels of resilience. Side Plate Systems brings a huge bonus to owners by delivering a lighter steel package, faster erection, and multiple areas of savings.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fe715bb e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"fe715bb\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f389131 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"f389131\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-3307 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2500px) 100vw, 2500px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png 2500w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-300x275.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1024x937.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-768x703.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1536x1406.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-2048x1874.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"2500\\\" height=\\\"2288\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481.png 2500w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-300x275.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1024x937.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-768x703.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-1536x1406.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/01\\/Side-plate-e1736663395481-2048x1874.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 2500px) 100vw, 2500px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d4d6fff e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d4d6fff\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-80e9291 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"80e9291\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section5\\\">5. CONCLUSION<\\/h2>\\n<div>In steel structures, quality connection design is crucial because connections are the points where individual members intersect and transfer loads. \\u00a0A well-thought-out connection improves the structure\\u2019s durability, safety, and integrity. <strong>By minimizing possible weak points, a high-quality connection design ensures effective force distribution and lowers the chance of failure under stresses like wind, seismic activity, and normal operation<\\/strong>. \\u00a0Additionally, good design simplifies the construction process, decreases maintenance needs, and ultimately saves costs. In summary, strong connections are essential to a successful and dependable steel construction because they guarantee that the structure will function as planned for its life.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1335,102,'_edit_last','1'),(1337,102,'_edit_lock','1746095607:1'),(1339,103,'_wp_old_date','2025-05-01'),(1340,2,'_elementor_css','a:6:{s:4:\"time\";i:1746095734;s:5:\"fonts\";a:2:{i:0;s:6:\"Roboto\";i:1;s:11:\"Roboto Slab\";}s:5:\"icons\";a: