r-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"c134fba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>Stairs play a crucial role in architecture, offering vertical connectivity between floors in multi-story buildings while fulfilling a functional purpose. Stairs are a structure that allows movement between different levels by dividing the vertical distance into smaller, manageable steps.<\\/p>\\n<p>Stairs encompass staircases, also called stairways, as well as escalators. Alternatives to traditional stairs include elevators (lifts), stair lifts, inclined moving walkways, ladders, and ramps.<\\/p>\\n<p>This article aims to highlight key aspects of stair codes relevant to steel detailing.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1ce422f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"1ce422f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f159939 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"f159939\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2>Table of Contents<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-5e86856 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-mobile__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"5e86856\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section1\\\">Introduction<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section2\\\">Stair Codes and Their Significance <\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section3\\\">Codes and Standards Applicable to Steel Detailing<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section4\\\">Conclusion<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3126a5f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"3126a5f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b99b920 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"b99b920\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section1\\\">1. INTRODUCTION<\\/h2>\\n<div>Stair codes play a vital role in safety, ensuring that stairs are designed to minimize the risk of falls and injuries. These regulations dictate key dimensions such as tread depth, riser height, and handrail specifications, all enforced to safeguard users.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d3ea5c7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"d3ea5c7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section2\\\">2. STAIR CODES AND THEIR IMPORTANCE<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>In the United States, stair detailing must adhere to various codes and standards to ensure safety, accessibility, and structural integrity. These regulations define essential aspects such as tread depth, riser height, handrails, and load-bearing requirements.<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Code Council was established in 1994, with the goal of developing a single set of national model construction codes. It brought together three different organizations that had developed three separate sets of model codes throughout the U.S.: Building Offi\\u00adcials and Code Administrators International, Inc. (BOCA), International Conference of Building Officials (ICBO) and Southern Building Code Congress International, Inc. (SBCCI).<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Building Code (IBC) and International Residential Code (IRC) are model building codes developed by the International Code Council (ICC) that are adopted by many jurisdictions in the US to ensure public safety and welfare in the built environment. The IBC applies to most structures, while the IRC specifically addresses one- and two-family dwellings.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-51aa218 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"51aa218\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section3\\\">3. CODES AND STANDARDS USED IN STEEL DETAILING<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>The following codes are applied in stair detailing:<\\/p>\\n<ol>\\n<li>IBC (International Building Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/li>\\n<li>ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/li>\\n<li>PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d1ec165 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d1ec165\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a49f34d e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"a49f34d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-88bd7bd elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"88bd7bd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5><strong>1. IBC (International Building Code)<\\/strong><\\/h5>\\n<p>The IBC is a model building code that provides a comprehensive set of guidelines for the design, construction, and safety of buildings, with the goal of protecting public health, safety, and welfare.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IBC Requirements for Stairways:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Width and Clearance<\\/strong>: Defines minimum stairway width for safe passage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Tread and Riser Dimensions<\\/strong>: Specifies uniform riser heights and tread depths for comfortable and secure movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Handrails and Guardrails<\\/strong>: Sets rules for placement, height, and design to enhance stability and prevent falls.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing and Platforms<\\/strong>: Regulates landing dimensions to provide resting points and safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Fire Safety and Egress<\\/strong>: Ensures stairways support emergency evacuation routes with proper fire-resistant materials and signage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Accessibility Compliance<\\/strong>: Aligns with ADA guidelines to accommodate users with mobility challenges.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ece6749 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"ece6749\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3421 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"AISC - Design_Guide - STAIR MINIMUM REQUIREMENT SKETCH\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d20752c e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d20752c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-97c617a elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"97c617a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">2. IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3ea0f4f e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"3ea0f4f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-27a8db1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"27a8db1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The International Residential Code (IRC) sets safety and design standards for stairways in residential buildings, ensuring they meet structural, accessibility, and usability requirements. These guidelines help prevent accidents and improve comfort in homes.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IRC Stairway Regulations:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Maximum Riser Height<\\/strong>: Defines the height of each step to maintain consistency and ease of movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Minimum Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Ensures sufficient foot space for stability while ascending or descending.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1d689e0 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"1d689e0\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3428 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"1024\\\" height=\\\"590\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f5666db e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"f5666db\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3780e4a elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"3780e4a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Handrail Requirements<\\/strong>: Specifies height and graspability for added safety and support.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Guardrail Standards<\\/strong>: Prevents falls by establishing minimum railing height and spacing.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing Dimensions<\\/strong>: Regulates the size and placement of stair landings for safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Headroom Clearance<\\/strong>: Ensures adequate overhead space to prevent obstructions.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>These IRC rules play a crucial role in designing residential stairways that are both functional and compliant with safety standards.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ce18657 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ce18657\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-adc4321 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"adc4321\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">3. OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-55edcc6 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"55edcc6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-56630d5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"56630d5\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) is a U.S. government agency responsible for ensuring safe and healthy working conditions. Established in 1970 under the Occupational Safety and Health Act, OSHA sets regulations and conducts inspections to protect workers across various industries.<\\/p>\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) standard 1910.25 outlines safety requirements for stairways in workplaces to prevent accidents and ensure structural integrity. These regulations apply to various stair types, including standard, spiral, ship, and alternating tread stairs.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-10bffc2 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"10bffc2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3432 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ada56dd e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ada56dd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fd0407a e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"fd0407a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0f39eee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"0f39eee\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default elementor-inline-editing pen\\\" contenteditable=\\\"true\\\" spellcheck=\\\"false\\\" data-elementor-setting-key=\\\"title\\\" data-pen-placeholder=\\\"Type Here...\\\" data-qb-tmp-id=\\\"lt-738382\\\" data-gramm=\\\"false\\\">4. ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)\\u200b<\\/h5>\\n<p>The Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) establishes accessibility standards for stairways to ensure safe and inclusive navigation for individuals with disabilities. These regulations apply to both interior and exterior stairs in public buildings and facilities.<br \\/>Key ADA Stairway Requirements:<br \\/><strong>Uniform Step Dimensions<\\/strong>: All steps must have consistent depth and height to prevent tripping hazards.<br \\/><strong>Step Height<\\/strong>: Must be between 5 and 7 inches for accessibility.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Minimum of 11 inches, measured from riser to riser, to provide secure footing.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Stair Width<\\/strong>: Must be at least 36 inches to accommodate users safely.<br \\/><strong>Handrails<\\/strong>: Required on both sides of stairways, positioned 34 to 38 inches above the stair nosing.<br \\/><strong>Nosings<\\/strong>: Must not project more than 1.5 inches beyond the riser below to reduce tripping risks.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-8baa50f elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"8baa50f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\u00a0<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-bbd2929 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"bbd2929\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c40a9f7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"c40a9f7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3469 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0c64e0e elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"0c64e0e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3465 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-57c9bd3 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"57c9bd3\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3477 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-e411696 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"e411696\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2fada2e elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"2fada2e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\"><br \\/>5. PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2e1c457 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"2e1c457\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>PIP Civil, Structural, and Architectural (CSA) Practices publishes essential CSA Engineering Design Practices, including specifications and fabrication\\/installation details.<\\/p>\\n<p>This Practice provides fabrication and installation details for standard pipe railing for walking and working surfaces and for stair railing or handrail for egress. Although the details in this practice are intended to meet U.S. Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) requirements for process facilities, they may not meet the requirements of local or national building codes.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-82239ba e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"82239ba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-125261c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"125261c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section4\\\">4. CONCLUSION<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>Building codes for stairs are established to enhance safety for all users, including children, the elderly, and individuals with disabilities.<\\/p>\\n<p>They help minimize the risks of slips, trips, and falls while ensuring uniformity in design and construction for both contractors and homeowners.<\\/p>\\n<p>The codes outlined above play a crucial role in stair design and construction, with periodic updates to accommodate evolving safety standards and requirements.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1372,813,'_wp_page_template','default'),(1373,813,'_thumbnail_id','653'),(1374,813,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1375,813,'_elementor_template_type','wp-post'),(1376,813,'_elementor_version','3.28.4'),(1377,813,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"640aad3e\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":[],\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"cffddfb\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"editor\":\"<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-644be11 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"644be11\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\" data-settings=\\\"{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c134fba elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"c134fba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>Stairs play a crucial role in architecture, offering vertical connectivity between floors in multi-story buildings while fulfilling a functional purpose. Stairs are a structure that allows movement between different levels by dividing the vertical distance into smaller, manageable steps.<\\/p>\\n<p>Stairs encompass staircases, also called stairways, as well as escalators. Alternatives to traditional stairs include elevators (lifts), stair lifts, inclined moving walkways, ladders, and ramps.<\\/p>\\n<p>This article aims to highlight key aspects of stair codes relevant to steel detailing.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1ce422f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"1ce422f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f159939 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"f159939\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2>Table of Contents<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-5e86856 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-mobile__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"5e86856\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section1\\\">Introduction<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section2\\\">Stair Codes and Their Significance <\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section3\\\">Codes and Standards Applicable to Steel Detailing<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section4\\\">Conclusion<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3126a5f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"3126a5f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b99b920 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"b99b920\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section1\\\">1. INTRODUCTION<\\/h2>\\n<div>Stair codes play a vital role in safety, ensuring that stairs are designed to minimize the risk of falls and injuries. These regulations dictate key dimensions such as tread depth, riser height, and handrail specifications, all enforced to safeguard users.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d3ea5c7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"d3ea5c7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section2\\\">2. STAIR CODES AND THEIR IMPORTANCE<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>In the United States, stair detailing must adhere to various codes and standards to ensure safety, accessibility, and structural integrity. These regulations define essential aspects such as tread depth, riser height, handrails, and load-bearing requirements.<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Code Council was established in 1994, with the goal of developing a single set of national model construction codes. It brought together three different organizations that had developed three separate sets of model codes throughout the U.S.: Building Offi\\u00adcials and Code Administrators International, Inc. (BOCA), International Conference of Building Officials (ICBO) and Southern Building Code Congress International, Inc. (SBCCI).<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Building Code (IBC) and International Residential Code (IRC) are model building codes developed by the International Code Council (ICC) that are adopted by many jurisdictions in the US to ensure public safety and welfare in the built environment. The IBC applies to most structures, while the IRC specifically addresses one- and two-family dwellings.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-51aa218 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"51aa218\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section3\\\">3. CODES AND STANDARDS USED IN STEEL DETAILING<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>The following codes are applied in stair detailing:<\\/p>\\n<ol>\\n<li>IBC (International Building Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/li>\\n<li>ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/li>\\n<li>PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d1ec165 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d1ec165\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a49f34d e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"a49f34d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-88bd7bd elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"88bd7bd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5><strong>1. IBC (International Building Code)<\\/strong><\\/h5>\\n<p>The IBC is a model building code that provides a comprehensive set of guidelines for the design, construction, and safety of buildings, with the goal of protecting public health, safety, and welfare.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IBC Requirements for Stairways:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Width and Clearance<\\/strong>: Defines minimum stairway width for safe passage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Tread and Riser Dimensions<\\/strong>: Specifies uniform riser heights and tread depths for comfortable and secure movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Handrails and Guardrails<\\/strong>: Sets rules for placement, height, and design to enhance stability and prevent falls.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing and Platforms<\\/strong>: Regulates landing dimensions to provide resting points and safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Fire Safety and Egress<\\/strong>: Ensures stairways support emergency evacuation routes with proper fire-resistant materials and signage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Accessibility Compliance<\\/strong>: Aligns with ADA guidelines to accommodate users with mobility challenges.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ece6749 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"ece6749\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3421 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"AISC - Design_Guide - STAIR MINIMUM REQUIREMENT SKETCH\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d20752c e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d20752c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-97c617a elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"97c617a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">2. IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3ea0f4f e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"3ea0f4f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-27a8db1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"27a8db1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The International Residential Code (IRC) sets safety and design standards for stairways in residential buildings, ensuring they meet structural, accessibility, and usability requirements. These guidelines help prevent accidents and improve comfort in homes.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IRC Stairway Regulations:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Maximum Riser Height<\\/strong>: Defines the height of each step to maintain consistency and ease of movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Minimum Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Ensures sufficient foot space for stability while ascending or descending.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1d689e0 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"1d689e0\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3428 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"1024\\\" height=\\\"590\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f5666db e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"f5666db\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3780e4a elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"3780e4a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Handrail Requirements<\\/strong>: Specifies height and graspability for added safety and support.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Guardrail Standards<\\/strong>: Prevents falls by establishing minimum railing height and spacing.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing Dimensions<\\/strong>: Regulates the size and placement of stair landings for safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Headroom Clearance<\\/strong>: Ensures adequate overhead space to prevent obstructions.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>These IRC rules play a crucial role in designing residential stairways that are both functional and compliant with safety standards.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ce18657 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ce18657\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-adc4321 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"adc4321\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">3. OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-55edcc6 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"55edcc6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-56630d5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"56630d5\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) is a U.S. government agency responsible for ensuring safe and healthy working conditions. Established in 1970 under the Occupational Safety and Health Act, OSHA sets regulations and conducts inspections to protect workers across various industries.<\\/p>\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) standard 1910.25 outlines safety requirements for stairways in workplaces to prevent accidents and ensure structural integrity. These regulations apply to various stair types, including standard, spiral, ship, and alternating tread stairs.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-10bffc2 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"10bffc2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3432 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ada56dd e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ada56dd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fd0407a e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"fd0407a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0f39eee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"0f39eee\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default elementor-inline-editing pen\\\" contenteditable=\\\"true\\\" spellcheck=\\\"false\\\" data-elementor-setting-key=\\\"title\\\" data-pen-placeholder=\\\"Type Here...\\\" data-qb-tmp-id=\\\"lt-738382\\\" data-gramm=\\\"false\\\">4. ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)\\u200b<\\/h5>\\n<p>The Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) establishes accessibility standards for stairways to ensure safe and inclusive navigation for individuals with disabilities. These regulations apply to both interior and exterior stairs in public buildings and facilities.<br \\/>Key ADA Stairway Requirements:<br \\/><strong>Uniform Step Dimensions<\\/strong>: All steps must have consistent depth and height to prevent tripping hazards.<br \\/><strong>Step Height<\\/strong>: Must be between 5 and 7 inches for accessibility.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Minimum of 11 inches, measured from riser to riser, to provide secure footing.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Stair Width<\\/strong>: Must be at least 36 inches to accommodate users safely.<br \\/><strong>Handrails<\\/strong>: Required on both sides of stairways, positioned 34 to 38 inches above the stair nosing.<br \\/><strong>Nosings<\\/strong>: Must not project more than 1.5 inches beyond the riser below to reduce tripping risks.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-8baa50f elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"8baa50f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3443 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-752x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 752px) 100vw, 752px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-752x1024.png 752w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-768x1046.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-1128x1536.png 1128w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-1504x2048.png 1504w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"752\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-752x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-752x1024.png 752w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-768x1046.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-1128x1536.png 1128w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-1504x2048.png 1504w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 752px) 100vw, 752px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-bbd2929 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"bbd2929\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c40a9f7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"c40a9f7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3469 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0c64e0e elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"0c64e0e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3465 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-57c9bd3 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"57c9bd3\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3477 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-e411696 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"e411696\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2fada2e elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"2fada2e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">5. PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2e1c457 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"2e1c457\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>PIP Civil, Structural, and Architectural (CSA) Practices publishes essential CSA Engineering Design Practices, including specifications and fabrication\\/installation details.<\\/p>\\n<p>This Practice provides fabrication and installation details for standard pipe railing for walking and working surfaces and for stair railing or handrail for egress. Although the details in this practice are intended to meet U.S. Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) requirements for process facilities, they may not meet the requirements of local or national building codes.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-82239ba e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"82239ba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-125261c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"125261c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section4\\\">4. CONCLUSION<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>Building codes for stairs are established to enhance safety for all users, including children, the elderly, and individuals with disabilities.<\\/p>\\n<p>They help minimize the risks of slips, trips, and falls while ensuring uniformity in design and construction for both contractors and homeowners.<\\/p>\\n<p>The codes outlined above play a crucial role in stair design and construction, with periodic updates to accommodate evolving safety standards and requirements.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1378,99,'_elementor_page_assets','a:0:{}'),(1382,814,'_wp_page_template','default'),(1383,814,'_thumbnail_id','653'),(1384,814,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1385,814,'_elementor_template_type','wp-post'),(1386,814,'_elementor_version','3.28.4'),(1387,814,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"640aad3e\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":[],\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"cffddfb\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"editor\":\"<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-644be11 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"644be11\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\" data-settings=\\\"{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c134fba elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"c134fba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>Stairs play a crucial role in architecture, offering vertical connectivity between floors in multi-story buildings while fulfilling a functional purpose. Stairs are a structure that allows movement between different levels by dividing the vertical distance into smaller, manageable steps.<\\/p>\\n<p>Stairs encompass staircases, also called stairways, as well as escalators. Alternatives to traditional stairs include elevators (lifts), stair lifts, inclined moving walkways, ladders, and ramps.<\\/p>\\n<p>This article aims to highlight key aspects of stair codes relevant to steel detailing.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1ce422f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"1ce422f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f159939 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"f159939\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2>Table of Contents<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-5e86856 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-mobile__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"5e86856\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section1\\\">Introduction<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section2\\\">Stair Codes and Their Significance <\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section3\\\">Codes and Standards Applicable to Steel Detailing<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section4\\\">Conclusion<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3126a5f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"3126a5f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b99b920 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"b99b920\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section1\\\">1. INTRODUCTION<\\/h2>\\n<div>Stair codes play a vital role in safety, ensuring that stairs are designed to minimize the risk of falls and injuries. These regulations dictate key dimensions such as tread depth, riser height, and handrail specifications, all enforced to safeguard users.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d3ea5c7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"d3ea5c7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section2\\\">2. STAIR CODES AND THEIR IMPORTANCE<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>In the United States, stair detailing must adhere to various codes and standards to ensure safety, accessibility, and structural integrity. These regulations define essential aspects such as tread depth, riser height, handrails, and load-bearing requirements.<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Code Council was established in 1994, with the goal of developing a single set of national model construction codes. It brought together three different organizations that had developed three separate sets of model codes throughout the U.S.: Building Offi\\u00adcials and Code Administrators International, Inc. (BOCA), International Conference of Building Officials (ICBO) and Southern Building Code Congress International, Inc. (SBCCI).<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Building Code (IBC) and International Residential Code (IRC) are model building codes developed by the International Code Council (ICC) that are adopted by many jurisdictions in the US to ensure public safety and welfare in the built environment. The IBC applies to most structures, while the IRC specifically addresses one- and two-family dwellings.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-51aa218 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"51aa218\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section3\\\">3. CODES AND STANDARDS USED IN STEEL DETAILING<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>The following codes are applied in stair detailing:<\\/p>\\n<ol>\\n<li>IBC (International Building Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/li>\\n<li>ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/li>\\n<li>PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d1ec165 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d1ec165\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a49f34d e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"a49f34d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-88bd7bd elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"88bd7bd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5><strong>1. IBC (International Building Code)<\\/strong><\\/h5>\\n<p>The IBC is a model building code that provides a comprehensive set of guidelines for the design, construction, and safety of buildings, with the goal of protecting public health, safety, and welfare.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IBC Requirements for Stairways:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Width and Clearance<\\/strong>: Defines minimum stairway width for safe passage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Tread and Riser Dimensions<\\/strong>: Specifies uniform riser heights and tread depths for comfortable and secure movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Handrails and Guardrails<\\/strong>: Sets rules for placement, height, and design to enhance stability and prevent falls.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing and Platforms<\\/strong>: Regulates landing dimensions to provide resting points and safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Fire Safety and Egress<\\/strong>: Ensures stairways support emergency evacuation routes with proper fire-resistant materials and signage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Accessibility Compliance<\\/strong>: Aligns with ADA guidelines to accommodate users with mobility challenges.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ece6749 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"ece6749\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3421 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"AISC - Design_Guide - STAIR MINIMUM REQUIREMENT SKETCH\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d20752c e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d20752c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-97c617a elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"97c617a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">2. IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3ea0f4f e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"3ea0f4f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-27a8db1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"27a8db1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The International Residential Code (IRC) sets safety and design standards for stairways in residential buildings, ensuring they meet structural, accessibility, and usability requirements. These guidelines help prevent accidents and improve comfort in homes.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IRC Stairway Regulations:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Maximum Riser Height<\\/strong>: Defines the height of each step to maintain consistency and ease of movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Minimum Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Ensures sufficient foot space for stability while ascending or descending.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1d689e0 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"1d689e0\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3428 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"1024\\\" height=\\\"590\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f5666db e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"f5666db\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3780e4a elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"3780e4a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Handrail Requirements<\\/strong>: Specifies height and graspability for added safety and support.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Guardrail Standards<\\/strong>: Prevents falls by establishing minimum railing height and spacing.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing Dimensions<\\/strong>: Regulates the size and placement of stair landings for safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Headroom Clearance<\\/strong>: Ensures adequate overhead space to prevent obstructions.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>These IRC rules play a crucial role in designing residential stairways that are both functional and compliant with safety standards.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ce18657 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ce18657\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-adc4321 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"adc4321\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">3. OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-55edcc6 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"55edcc6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-56630d5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"56630d5\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) is a U.S. government agency responsible for ensuring safe and healthy working conditions. Established in 1970 under the Occupational Safety and Health Act, OSHA sets regulations and conducts inspections to protect workers across various industries.<\\/p>\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) standard 1910.25 outlines safety requirements for stairways in workplaces to prevent accidents and ensure structural integrity. These regulations apply to various stair types, including standard, spiral, ship, and alternating tread stairs.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-10bffc2 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"10bffc2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3432 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ada56dd e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ada56dd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fd0407a e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"fd0407a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0f39eee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"0f39eee\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default elementor-inline-editing pen\\\" contenteditable=\\\"true\\\" spellcheck=\\\"false\\\" data-elementor-setting-key=\\\"title\\\" data-pen-placeholder=\\\"Type Here...\\\" data-qb-tmp-id=\\\"lt-738382\\\" data-gramm=\\\"false\\\">4. ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)\\u200b<\\/h5>\\n<p>The Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) establishes accessibility standards for stairways to ensure safe and inclusive navigation for individuals with disabilities. These regulations apply to both interior and exterior stairs in public buildings and facilities.<br \\/>Key ADA Stairway Requirements:<br \\/><strong>Uniform Step Dimensions<\\/strong>: All steps must have consistent depth and height to prevent tripping hazards.<br \\/><strong>Step Height<\\/strong>: Must be between 5 and 7 inches for accessibility.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Minimum of 11 inches, measured from riser to riser, to provide secure footing.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Stair Width<\\/strong>: Must be at least 36 inches to accommodate users safely.<br \\/><strong>Handrails<\\/strong>: Required on both sides of stairways, positioned 34 to 38 inches above the stair nosing.<br \\/><strong>Nosings<\\/strong>: Must not project more than 1.5 inches beyond the riser below to reduce tripping risks.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-8baa50f elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"8baa50f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3443 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-752x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 752px) 100vw, 752px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-752x1024.png 752w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-768x1046.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-1128x1536.png 1128w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-1504x2048.png 1504w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"752\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-752x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-752x1024.png 752w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-768x1046.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-1128x1536.png 1128w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-1504x2048.png 1504w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 752px) 100vw, 752px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-bbd2929 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"bbd2929\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c40a9f7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"c40a9f7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3469 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0c64e0e elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"0c64e0e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3465 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-57c9bd3 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"57c9bd3\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3477 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-e411696 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"e411696\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2fada2e elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"2fada2e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">5. PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2e1c457 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"2e1c457\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>PIP Civil, Structural, and Architectural (CSA) Practices publishes essential CSA Engineering Design Practices, including specifications and fabrication\\/installation details.<\\/p>\\n<p>This Practice provides fabrication and installation details for standard pipe railing for walking and working surfaces and for stair railing or handrail for egress. Although the details in this practice are intended to meet U.S. Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) requirements for process facilities, they may not meet the requirements of local or national building codes.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-82239ba e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"82239ba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-125261c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"125261c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section4\\\">4. CONCLUSION<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>Building codes for stairs are established to enhance safety for all users, including children, the elderly, and individuals with disabilities.<\\/p>\\n<p>They help minimize the risks of slips, trips, and falls while ensuring uniformity in design and construction for both contractors and homeowners.<\\/p>\\n<p>The codes outlined above play a crucial role in stair design and construction, with periodic updates to accommodate evolving safety standards and requirements.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1388,814,'_elementor_page_assets','a:0:{}'),(1389,814,'_elementor_css','a:6:{s:4:\"time\";i:1746095873;s:5:\"fonts\";a:0:{}s:5:\"icons\";a:0:{}s:20:\"dynamic_elements_ids\";a:0:{}s:6:\"status\";s:4:\"file\";i:0;s:0:\"\";}'),(1390,814,'_elementor_element_cache','{\"timeout\":1746182273,\"value\":{\"content\":\"<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-640aad3e e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"640aad3e\" data-element_type=\"container\">nttttt<div class=\"e-con-inner\">ntt[elementor-element data=\"\"]ttt</div>ntttt</div>ntt\",\"scripts\":[],\"styles\":[]}}'),(1391,815,'_wp_page_template','default'),(1392,815,'_thumbnail_id','653'),(1393,815,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1394,815,'_elementor_template_type','wp-post'),(1395,815,'_elementor_version','3.28.4'),(1396,815,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"640aad3e\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":[],\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"cffddfb\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"editor\":\"<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-644be11 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"644be11\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\" data-settings=\\\"{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c134fba elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"c134fba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>Stairs play a crucial role in architecture, offering vertical connectivity between floors in multi-story buildings while fulfilling a functional purpose. Stairs are a structure that allows movement between different levels by dividing the vertical distance into smaller, manageable steps.<\\/p>\\n<p>Stairs encompass staircases, also called stairways, as well as escalators. Alternatives to traditional stairs include elevators (lifts), stair lifts, inclined moving walkways, ladders, and ramps.<\\/p>\\n<p>This article aims to highlight key aspects of stair codes relevant to steel detailing.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1ce422f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"1ce422f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f159939 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"f159939\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2>Table of Contents<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-5e86856 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-mobile__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"5e86856\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section1\\\">Introduction<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section2\\\">Stair Codes and Their Significance <\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section3\\\">Codes and Standards Applicable to Steel Detailing<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section4\\\">Conclusion<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3126a5f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"3126a5f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b99b920 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"b99b920\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section1\\\">1. INTRODUCTION<\\/h2>\\n<div>Stair codes play a vital role in safety, ensuring that stairs are designed to minimize the risk of falls and injuries. These regulations dictate key dimensions such as tread depth, riser height, and handrail specifications, all enforced to safeguard users.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d3ea5c7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"d3ea5c7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section2\\\">2. STAIR CODES AND THEIR IMPORTANCE<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>In the United States, stair detailing must adhere to various codes and standards to ensure safety, accessibility, and structural integrity. These regulations define essential aspects such as tread depth, riser height, handrails, and load-bearing requirements.<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Code Council was established in 1994, with the goal of developing a single set of national model construction codes. It brought together three different organizations that had developed three separate sets of model codes throughout the U.S.: Building Offi\\u00adcials and Code Administrators International, Inc. (BOCA), International Conference of Building Officials (ICBO) and Southern Building Code Congress International, Inc. (SBCCI).<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Building Code (IBC) and International Residential Code (IRC) are model building codes developed by the International Code Council (ICC) that are adopted by many jurisdictions in the US to ensure public safety and welfare in the built environment. The IBC applies to most structures, while the IRC specifically addresses one- and two-family dwellings.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-51aa218 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"51aa218\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section3\\\">3. CODES AND STANDARDS USED IN STEEL DETAILING<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>The following codes are applied in stair detailing:<\\/p>\\n<ol>\\n<li>IBC (International Building Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/li>\\n<li>ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/li>\\n<li>PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d1ec165 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d1ec165\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a49f34d e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"a49f34d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-88bd7bd elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"88bd7bd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5><strong>1. IBC (International Building Code)<\\/strong><\\/h5>\\n<p>The IBC is a model building code that provides a comprehensive set of guidelines for the design, construction, and safety of buildings, with the goal of protecting public health, safety, and welfare.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IBC Requirements for Stairways:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Width and Clearance<\\/strong>: Defines minimum stairway width for safe passage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Tread and Riser Dimensions<\\/strong>: Specifies uniform riser heights and tread depths for comfortable and secure movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Handrails and Guardrails<\\/strong>: Sets rules for placement, height, and design to enhance stability and prevent falls.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing and Platforms<\\/strong>: Regulates landing dimensions to provide resting points and safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Fire Safety and Egress<\\/strong>: Ensures stairways support emergency evacuation routes with proper fire-resistant materials and signage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Accessibility Compliance<\\/strong>: Aligns with ADA guidelines to accommodate users with mobility challenges.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ece6749 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"ece6749\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3421 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"AISC - Design_Guide - STAIR MINIMUM REQUIREMENT SKETCH\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d20752c e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d20752c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-97c617a elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"97c617a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">2. IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3ea0f4f e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"3ea0f4f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-27a8db1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"27a8db1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The International Residential Code (IRC) sets safety and design standards for stairways in residential buildings, ensuring they meet structural, accessibility, and usability requirements. These guidelines help prevent accidents and improve comfort in homes.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IRC Stairway Regulations:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Maximum Riser Height<\\/strong>: Defines the height of each step to maintain consistency and ease of movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Minimum Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Ensures sufficient foot space for stability while ascending or descending.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1d689e0 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"1d689e0\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3428 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"1024\\\" height=\\\"590\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f5666db e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"f5666db\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3780e4a elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"3780e4a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Handrail Requirements<\\/strong>: Specifies height and graspability for added safety and support.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Guardrail Standards<\\/strong>: Prevents falls by establishing minimum railing height and spacing.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing Dimensions<\\/strong>: Regulates the size and placement of stair landings for safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Headroom Clearance<\\/strong>: Ensures adequate overhead space to prevent obstructions.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>These IRC rules play a crucial role in designing residential stairways that are both functional and compliant with safety standards.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ce18657 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ce18657\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-adc4321 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"adc4321\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">3. OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-55edcc6 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"55edcc6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-56630d5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"56630d5\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) is a U.S. government agency responsible for ensuring safe and healthy working conditions. Established in 1970 under the Occupational Safety and Health Act, OSHA sets regulations and conducts inspections to protect workers across various industries.<\\/p>\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) standard 1910.25 outlines safety requirements for stairways in workplaces to prevent accidents and ensure structural integrity. These regulations apply to various stair types, including standard, spiral, ship, and alternating tread stairs.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-10bffc2 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"10bffc2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3432 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ada56dd e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ada56dd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fd0407a e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"fd0407a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0f39eee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"0f39eee\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default elementor-inline-editing pen\\\" contenteditable=\\\"true\\\" spellcheck=\\\"false\\\" data-elementor-setting-key=\\\"title\\\" data-pen-placeholder=\\\"Type Here...\\\" data-qb-tmp-id=\\\"lt-738382\\\" data-gramm=\\\"false\\\">4. ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)\\u200b<\\/h5>\\n<p>The Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) establishes accessibility standards for stairways to ensure safe and inclusive navigation for individuals with disabilities. These regulations apply to both interior and exterior stairs in public buildings and facilities.<br \\/>Key ADA Stairway Requirements:<br \\/><strong>Uniform Step Dimensions<\\/strong>: All steps must have consistent depth and height to prevent tripping hazards.<br \\/><strong>Step Height<\\/strong>: Must be between 5 and 7 inches for accessibility.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Minimum of 11 inches, measured from riser to riser, to provide secure footing.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Stair Width<\\/strong>: Must be at least 36 inches to accommodate users safely.<br \\/><strong>Handrails<\\/strong>: Required on both sides of stairways, positioned 34 to 38 inches above the stair nosing.<br \\/><strong>Nosings<\\/strong>: Must not project more than 1.5 inches beyond the riser below to reduce tripping risks.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-8baa50f elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"8baa50f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3443 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-752x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 752px) 100vw, 752px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-752x1024.png 752w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-768x1046.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-1128x1536.png 1128w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-1504x2048.png 1504w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"752\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-752x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-752x1024.png 752w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-768x1046.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-1128x1536.png 1128w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stairway-handrails-1504x2048.png 1504w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 752px) 100vw, 752px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-bbd2929 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"bbd2929\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c40a9f7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"c40a9f7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3469 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0c64e0e elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"0c64e0e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3465 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-57c9bd3 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"57c9bd3\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3477 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-e411696 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"e411696\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2fada2e elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"2fada2e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">5. PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2e1c457 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"2e1c457\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>PIP Civil, Structural, and Architectural (CSA) Practices publishes essential CSA Engineering Design Practices, including specifications and fabrication\\/installation details.<\\/p>\\n<p>This Practice provides fabrication and installation details for standard pipe railing for walking and working surfaces and for stair railing or handrail for egress. Although the details in this practice are intended to meet U.S. Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) requirements for process facilities, they may not meet the requirements of local or national building codes.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-82239ba e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"82239ba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-125261c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"125261c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section4\\\">4. CONCLUSION<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>Building codes for stairs are established to enhance safety for all users, including children, the elderly, and individuals with disabilities.<\\/p>\\n<p>They help minimize the risks of slips, trips, and falls while ensuring uniformity in design and construction for both contractors and homeowners.<\\/p>\\n<p>The codes outlined above play a crucial role in stair design and construction, with periodic updates to accommodate evolving safety standards and requirements.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1397,815,'_elementor_page_assets','a:0:{}'),(1398,815,'_elementor_css','a:6:{s:4:\"time\";i:1746095873;s:5:\"fonts\";a:0:{}s:5:\"icons\";a:0:{}s:20:\"dynamic_elements_ids\";a:0:{}s:6:\"status\";s:4:\"file\";i:0;s:0:\"\";}'),(1399,815,'_elementor_element_cache','{\"timeout\":1746182273,\"value\":{\"content\":\"<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-640aad3e e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"640aad3e\" data-element_type=\"container\">nttttt<div class=\"e-con-inner\">ntt[elementor-element data=\"\"]ttt</div>ntttt</div>ntt\",\"scripts\":[],\"styles\":[]}}'),(1400,816,'_wp_page_template','default'),(1401,816,'_thumbnail_id','653'),(1402,816,'_elementor_edit_mode','builder'),(1403,816,'_elementor_template_type','wp-post'),(1404,816,'_elementor_version','3.28.4'),(1405,816,'_elementor_data','[{\"id\":\"640aad3e\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":[],\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"cffddfb\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"editor\":\"<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-644be11 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"644be11\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\" data-settings=\\\"{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c134fba elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"c134fba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>Stairs play a crucial role in architecture, offering vertical connectivity between floors in multi-story buildings while fulfilling a functional purpose. Stairs are a structure that allows movement between different levels by dividing the vertical distance into smaller, manageable steps.<\\/p>\\n<p>Stairs encompass staircases, also called stairways, as well as escalators. Alternatives to traditional stairs include elevators (lifts), stair lifts, inclined moving walkways, ladders, and ramps.<\\/p>\\n<p>This article aims to highlight key aspects of stair codes relevant to steel detailing.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1ce422f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"1ce422f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f159939 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"f159939\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2>Table of Contents<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-5e86856 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget-mobile__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-html\\\" data-id=\\\"5e86856\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"html.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section1\\\">Introduction<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section2\\\">Stair Codes and Their Significance <\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section3\\\">Codes and Standards Applicable to Steel Detailing<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/stair-code-standards-in-steel-detailing\\/#section4\\\">Conclusion<\\/a><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3126a5f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"3126a5f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-b99b920 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"b99b920\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section1\\\">1. INTRODUCTION<\\/h2>\\n<div>Stair codes play a vital role in safety, ensuring that stairs are designed to minimize the risk of falls and injuries. These regulations dictate key dimensions such as tread depth, riser height, and handrail specifications, all enforced to safeguard users.<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d3ea5c7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"d3ea5c7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section2\\\">2. STAIR CODES AND THEIR IMPORTANCE<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>In the United States, stair detailing must adhere to various codes and standards to ensure safety, accessibility, and structural integrity. These regulations define essential aspects such as tread depth, riser height, handrails, and load-bearing requirements.<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Code Council was established in 1994, with the goal of developing a single set of national model construction codes. It brought together three different organizations that had developed three separate sets of model codes throughout the U.S.: Building Offi\\u00adcials and Code Administrators International, Inc. (BOCA), International Conference of Building Officials (ICBO) and Southern Building Code Congress International, Inc. (SBCCI).<\\/p>\\n<p>The International Building Code (IBC) and International Residential Code (IRC) are model building codes developed by the International Code Council (ICC) that are adopted by many jurisdictions in the US to ensure public safety and welfare in the built environment. The IBC applies to most structures, while the IRC specifically addresses one- and two-family dwellings.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-51aa218 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"51aa218\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section3\\\">3. CODES AND STANDARDS USED IN STEEL DETAILING<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>The following codes are applied in stair detailing:<\\/p>\\n<ol>\\n<li>IBC (International Building Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/li>\\n<li>OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/li>\\n<li>ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)<\\/li>\\n<li>PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d1ec165 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d1ec165\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-a49f34d e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"a49f34d\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-88bd7bd elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"88bd7bd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5><strong>1. IBC (International Building Code)<\\/strong><\\/h5>\\n<p>The IBC is a model building code that provides a comprehensive set of guidelines for the design, construction, and safety of buildings, with the goal of protecting public health, safety, and welfare.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IBC Requirements for Stairways:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Width and Clearance<\\/strong>: Defines minimum stairway width for safe passage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Tread and Riser Dimensions<\\/strong>: Specifies uniform riser heights and tread depths for comfortable and secure movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Handrails and Guardrails<\\/strong>: Sets rules for placement, height, and design to enhance stability and prevent falls.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing and Platforms<\\/strong>: Regulates landing dimensions to provide resting points and safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Fire Safety and Egress<\\/strong>: Ensures stairways support emergency evacuation routes with proper fire-resistant materials and signage.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Accessibility Compliance<\\/strong>: Aligns with ADA guidelines to accommodate users with mobility challenges.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ece6749 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"ece6749\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3421 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"AISC - Design_Guide - STAIR MINIMUM REQUIREMENT SKETCH\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/New-Project-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-d20752c e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"d20752c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-97c617a elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"97c617a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">2. IRC (International Residential Code)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3ea0f4f e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"3ea0f4f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-27a8db1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"27a8db1\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The International Residential Code (IRC) sets safety and design standards for stairways in residential buildings, ensuring they meet structural, accessibility, and usability requirements. These guidelines help prevent accidents and improve comfort in homes.<\\/p>\\n<p>Key IRC Stairway Regulations:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Maximum Riser Height<\\/strong>: Defines the height of each step to maintain consistency and ease of movement.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Minimum Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Ensures sufficient foot space for stability while ascending or descending.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-1d689e0 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"1d689e0\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3428 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"1024\\\" height=\\\"590\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1024x590.png 1024w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-300x173.png 300w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-768x443.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-1536x885.png 1536w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Stair-Code-Standards-in-Steel-Detailing-BLOG-002_1-2048x1181.png 2048w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-f5666db e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"f5666db\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-3780e4a elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"3780e4a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Handrail Requirements<\\/strong>: Specifies height and graspability for added safety and support.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Guardrail Standards<\\/strong>: Prevents falls by establishing minimum railing height and spacing.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Landing Dimensions<\\/strong>: Regulates the size and placement of stair landings for safe transitions.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Headroom Clearance<\\/strong>: Ensures adequate overhead space to prevent obstructions.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>These IRC rules play a crucial role in designing residential stairways that are both functional and compliant with safety standards.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ce18657 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ce18657\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-adc4321 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"adc4321\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\">3. OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-55edcc6 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"55edcc6\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-56630d5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"56630d5\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) is a U.S. government agency responsible for ensuring safe and healthy working conditions. Established in 1970 under the Occupational Safety and Health Act, OSHA sets regulations and conducts inspections to protect workers across various industries.<\\/p>\\n<p>The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) standard 1910.25 outlines safety requirements for stairways in workplaces to prevent accidents and ensure structural integrity. These regulations apply to various stair types, including standard, spiral, ship, and alternating tread stairs.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-10bffc2 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"10bffc2\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3432 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"751\\\" height=\\\"1024\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-751x1024.png 751w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-220x300.png 220w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-768x1048.png 768w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1126x1536.png 1126w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/AISC-Design_Guide_34-STAIR-MINIMUM-REQUIREMENT-SKETCH-1_2-1501x2048.png 1501w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 751px) 100vw, 751px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-ada56dd e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"ada56dd\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-fd0407a e-grid e-con-full e-con e-child\\\" data-id=\\\"fd0407a\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0f39eee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"0f39eee\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h5 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default elementor-inline-editing pen\\\" contenteditable=\\\"true\\\" spellcheck=\\\"false\\\" data-elementor-setting-key=\\\"title\\\" data-pen-placeholder=\\\"Type Here...\\\" data-qb-tmp-id=\\\"lt-738382\\\" data-gramm=\\\"false\\\">4. ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)\\u200b<\\/h5>\\n<p>The Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) establishes accessibility standards for stairways to ensure safe and inclusive navigation for individuals with disabilities. These regulations apply to both interior and exterior stairs in public buildings and facilities.<br \\/>Key ADA Stairway Requirements:<br \\/><strong>Uniform Step Dimensions<\\/strong>: All steps must have consistent depth and height to prevent tripping hazards.<br \\/><strong>Step Height<\\/strong>: Must be between 5 and 7 inches for accessibility.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Tread Depth<\\/strong>: Minimum of 11 inches, measured from riser to riser, to provide secure footing.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Stair Width<\\/strong>: Must be at least 36 inches to accommodate users safely.<br \\/><strong>Handrails<\\/strong>: Required on both sides of stairways, positioned 34 to 38 inches above the stair nosing.<br \\/><strong>Nosings<\\/strong>: Must not project more than 1.5 inches beyond the riser below to reduce tripping risks.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-8baa50f elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"8baa50f\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\u00a0<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-bbd2929 e-grid e-con-full e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"bbd2929\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-c40a9f7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"c40a9f7\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3469 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Top-handrail-Extension-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-0c64e0e elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"0c64e0e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3465 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Bottom-handrail-Extension-1-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-57c9bd3 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\\\" data-id=\\\"57c9bd3\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"image.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\"><img class=\\\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3477 entered litespeed-loaded\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"473\\\" height=\\\"512\\\" data-lazyloaded=\\\"1\\\" data-src=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png\\\" data-srcset=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy.png 473w, https:\\/\\/www.esskaystructures.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/handrail-Extension-2-Copy-277x300.png 277w\\\" data-sizes=\\\"(max-width: 473px) 100vw, 473px\\\" data-ll-status=\\\"loaded\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-e411696 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"e411696\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2fada2e elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\\\" data-id=\\\"2fada2e\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"heading.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 class=\\\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\\\"><br \\/>5. PIP (Process Industry Practices)<\\/h2>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-2e1c457 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"2e1c457\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<p>PIP Civil, Structural, and Architectural (CSA) Practices publishes essential CSA Engineering Design Practices, including specifications and fabrication\\/installation details.<\\/p>\\n<p>This Practice provides fabrication and installation details for standard pipe railing for walking and working surfaces and for stair railing or handrail for egress. Although the details in this practice are intended to meet U.S. Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) requirements for process facilities, they may not meet the requirements of local or national building codes.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-82239ba e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded\\\" data-id=\\\"82239ba\\\" data-element_type=\\\"container\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"e-con-inner\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-element elementor-element-125261c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\\\" data-id=\\\"125261c\\\" data-element_type=\\\"widget\\\" data-widget_type=\\\"text-editor.default\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"elementor-widget-container\\\">\\n<h2 id=\\\"section4\\\">4. CONCLUSION<\\/h2>\\n<div>\\n<p>Building codes for stairs are established to enhance safety for all users, including children, the elderly, and individuals with disabilities.<\\/p>\\n<p>They help minimize the risks of slips, trips, and falls while ensuring uniformity in design and construction for both contractors and homeowners.<\\/p>\\n<p>The codes outlined above play a crucial role in stair design and construction, with periodic updates to accommodate evolving safety standards and requirements.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\"},\"elements\":[],\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\"}],\"isInner\":false}]'),(1406,816,'_elementor_page_assets','a:0:{}'),(1407,816,'_elementor_css','a:6:{s:4:\"time\";i:1746095873;s:5:\"fonts\";a:0:{}s:5:\"icons\";a:0:{}s:20:\"dynamic_elements_ids\";a:0:{}s:6:\"status\";s:4:\"file\";i:0;s:0:\"\";}'),(1408,816,'_elementor_element_cache','{\"timeout\":1746182273,\"value\":{\"content\":\"<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-640aad3e e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"640aad3e\" data-element_type=\"container\">nttttt<div class=\"e-con-inner\">ntt[elementor-element data=\"\"]ttt</div>ntttt</div>ntt\",\"scripts\":[],\"styles\":[]}}'),(1409,99,'_elementor_css','a:6:{s:4:\"time\";i:1746095928;s:5:\"fonts\";a:0:{}s:5:\"icons\";a:0:{}s:20:\"dynamic_elements_ids\";a:0:{}s:6:\"status\";s:4:\"file\";i:0;s:0:\"\";}');
